1
00:00:28,110 --> 00:00:30,660
The Tesseract has awakened.

2
00:00:33,120 --> 00:00:38,070
It is on a little world, a human world.

3
00:00:38,790 --> 00:00:42,120
They would wield its power,

4
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:48,160
but our ally knows its workings as they never will.

5
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:52,790
He is ready to lead

6
00:00:53,010 --> 00:00:58,430
and our force, our Chitauri, will follow.

7
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:02,430
A world will be his.

8
00:01:02,650 --> 00:01:05,770
The universe, yours.

9
00:01:05,990 --> 00:01:10,820
And the humans, what can they do but burn?

10
00:01:26,090 --> 00:01:29,630
All personnel, the evacuation order has been confirmed...

11
00:02:01,550 --> 00:02:03,000
How bad is it?

12
00:02:03,220 --> 00:02:06,500
That's the problem, sir. We don't know.

13
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:13,010
Dr Selvig read an energy surge from the Tesseract four hours ago.

14
00:02:13,150 --> 00:02:15,010
NASA didn't authorise Selvig to go to test phase.

15
00:02:15,230 --> 00:02:17,390
He wasn't testing it. He wasn't even in the room.

16
00:02:17,610 --> 00:02:18,600
Spontaneous event.

17
00:02:18,780 --> 00:02:19,880
It just turned itself on?

18
00:02:20,110 --> 00:02:21,140
Where are the energy levels now?

19
00:02:21,370 --> 00:02:23,520
Climbing. When Selvig couldn't shut it down, we ordered evac.

20
00:02:23,740 --> 00:02:24,830
How long to get everyone out?

21
00:02:24,830 --> 00:02:26,490
Campus should be clear in the next half-hour.

22
00:02:26,700 --> 00:02:27,950
Do better.

23
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:30,870
Sir, evacuation may be futile.

24
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:32,450
We should tell them to go back to sleep?

25
00:02:32,670 --> 00:02:37,410
If we can't control the Tesseract's energy, there may not be a minimum safe distance.

26
00:02:37,550 --> 00:02:40,380
I need you to make sure the Phase 2 prototypes are shipped out.

27
00:02:40,550 --> 00:02:42,590
Sir, is that really a priority right now?

28
00:02:42,810 --> 00:02:44,510
Until such time as the world ends,

29
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:46,680
we will act as though it intends to spin on.

30
00:02:47,650 --> 00:02:49,010
Clear out the tech below.

31
00:02:49,230 --> 00:02:51,710
Every piece of Phase 2 on a truck and gone.

32
00:02:51,940 --> 00:02:53,020
Yes, sir.

33
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:54,180
With me.

34
00:02:57,700 --> 00:02:58,690
Talk to me, Doctor.

35
00:03:00,490 --> 00:03:01,860
Director.

36
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:03,740
Is there anything we know for certain?

37
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:05,680
The Tesseract is misbehaving.

38
00:03:06,420 --> 00:03:07,320
Is that supposed to be funny?

39
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:08,790
No, it's not funny at all.

40
00:03:09,420 --> 00:03:12,910
The Tesseract is not only active, she's behaving.

41
00:03:13,130 --> 00:03:14,120
I assume you pulled the plug.

42
00:03:14,340 --> 00:03:16,040
She's an energy source.

43
00:03:16,260 --> 00:03:19,300
We turn off the power, she turns it back on.

44
00:03:19,510 --> 00:03:20,590
If she reaches peak level...

45
00:03:20,810 --> 00:03:24,220
We prepared for this, Doctor. Harnessing energy from space.

46
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:25,800
But we don't have the harness.

47
00:03:25,940 --> 00:03:27,210
My calculations are far from complete.

48
00:03:27,770 --> 00:03:30,310
And she's throwing off interference, radiation.

49
00:03:30,530 --> 00:03:32,230
Nothing harmful, low levels of gamma radiation.

50
00:03:33,160 --> 00:03:34,980
That can be harmful.

51
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:36,610
Where's Agent Barton?

52
00:03:36,780 --> 00:03:38,480
The Hawk?

53
00:03:39,370 --> 00:03:41,400
Up in his nest, as usual.

54
00:03:42,870 --> 00:03:44,660
Agent Barton, report.

55
00:03:45,540 --> 00:03:48,410
I gave you this detail, so you could keep a close eye on things.

56
00:03:48,630 --> 00:03:50,000
Well, I see better from a distance.

57
00:03:50,220 --> 00:03:52,170
Have you seen anything that might set this thing off?

58
00:03:52,640 --> 00:03:54,750
Doctor, it's spiking again.

59
00:03:54,970 --> 00:03:56,340
No one's come or gone.

60
00:03:56,560 --> 00:03:58,170
And Selvig's clean.

61
00:03:58,390 --> 00:04:00,680
No contacts, no IMs.

62
00:04:01,190 --> 00:04:02,970
If there was any tampering, sir, it wasn't at this end.

63
00:04:04,900 --> 00:04:06,270
"At this end"?

64
00:04:06,490 --> 00:04:10,310
Yeah, the Cube is a doorway to the other end of space, right?

65
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:13,430
Doors open from both sides.

66
00:04:14,200 --> 00:04:15,530
Not yet.

67
00:05:23,450 --> 00:05:26,570
Sir, please put down the spear.

68
00:06:05,910 --> 00:06:07,070
You have heart.

69
00:06:37,660 --> 00:06:39,150
Please don't.

70
00:06:40,950 --> 00:06:42,140
I still need that.

71
00:06:42,370 --> 00:06:43,820
This doesn't have to get any messier.

72
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:45,230
Of course it does.

73
00:06:45,460 --> 00:06:47,330
I've come too far for anything else.

74
00:06:49,300 --> 00:06:52,080
I am Loki, of Asgard

75
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:55,170
and I am burdened with glorious purpose.

76
00:06:55,390 --> 00:06:56,790
Loki,

77
00:06:57,310 --> 00:06:58,580
brother of Thor.

78
00:06:58,810 --> 00:07:01,260
We have no quarrel with your people.

79
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:04,430
An ant has no quarrel with a boot.

80
00:07:05,020 --> 00:07:06,680
Are you planning to step on us?

81
00:07:07,030 --> 00:07:10,100
I come with glad tidings

82
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:13,270
of a world made free.

83
00:07:13,660 --> 00:07:14,650
Free from what?

84
00:07:14,870 --> 00:07:16,190
Freedom.

85
00:07:16,740 --> 00:07:19,360
Freedom is life's great lie.

86
00:07:19,580 --> 00:07:22,990
Once you accept that, in your heart,

87
00:07:27,510 --> 00:07:29,370
you will know peace.

88
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:32,130
Yeah, you say "peace,"

89
00:07:32,350 --> 00:07:34,170
I kind of think you mean the other thing.

90
00:07:34,390 --> 00:07:36,870
Sir, Director Fury is stalling.

91
00:07:37,100 --> 00:07:38,430
This place is about to blow

92
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:40,260
and drop a hundred feet of rock on us.

93
00:07:41,770 --> 00:07:42,800
He means to bury us.

94
00:07:43,020 --> 00:07:44,130
Like the pharaohs of old.

95
00:07:44,360 --> 00:07:46,310
He's right. The portal is collapsing in on itself.

96
00:07:46,530 --> 00:07:48,730
We've got maybe two minutes before this goes critical.

97
00:07:49,110 --> 00:07:50,110
Well, then.

98
00:08:05,880 --> 00:08:06,960
I need these vehicles.

99
00:08:11,060 --> 00:08:11,820
Who's that?

100
00:08:12,120 --> 00:08:13,170
They didn't tell me.

101
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:17,640
Hill!

102
00:08:18,060 --> 00:08:19,340
Do you copy?

103
00:08:20,070 --> 00:08:21,390
Barton has turned.

104
00:08:34,460 --> 00:08:37,280
They have the Tesseract! Shut them down!

105
00:09:13,710 --> 00:09:15,910
Okay, let's go. No, leave it. Go!

106
00:09:32,400 --> 00:09:34,520
We're clear upstairs, sir. You need to go.

107
00:11:06,510 --> 00:11:07,830
Director?

108
00:11:08,180 --> 00:11:09,670
Director Fury, do you copy?

109
00:11:09,890 --> 00:11:12,170
The Tesseract is with a hostile force.

110
00:11:12,430 --> 00:11:14,830
I have men down. Hill?

111
00:11:15,180 --> 00:11:17,050
A lot of men still under.

112
00:11:17,270 --> 00:11:18,970
I don't know how many survivors.

113
00:11:19,190 --> 00:11:20,350
Sound a general call.

114
00:11:20,560 --> 00:11:23,390
I want every living soul not working rescue looking for that briefcase.

115
00:11:23,610 --> 00:11:24,630
Roger that.

116
00:11:24,860 --> 00:11:28,150
Coulson, get back to base. This is a Level Seven.

117
00:11:29,240 --> 00:11:30,820
As of right now,

118
00:11:31,040 --> 00:11:32,480
we are at war.

119
00:11:34,210 --> 00:11:35,480
What do we do?

120
00:12:12,370 --> 00:12:16,070
This is not how I wanted this evening to go.

121
00:12:16,210 --> 00:12:17,830
I know how you wanted this evening to go.

122
00:12:18,050 --> 00:12:20,280
Believe me, this is better.

123
00:12:21,260 --> 00:12:23,130
Who are you working for?

124
00:12:23,510 --> 00:12:25,090
Lermentov, yes?

125
00:12:27,060 --> 00:12:32,680
Does he think we have to go through him to move our cargo?

126
00:12:33,940 --> 00:12:38,480
I thought General Solohob is in charge of the export business.

127
00:12:38,820 --> 00:12:40,770
Solohob

128
00:12:40,990 --> 00:12:43,020
a bagman, a front.

129
00:12:45,500 --> 00:12:49,660
Your outdated information betrays you.

130
00:12:51,250 --> 00:12:53,990
The famous Black Widow

131
00:12:55,670 --> 00:13:00,040
and she turns out to be simply another pretty face.

132
00:13:00,930 --> 00:13:04,090
You really think I'm pretty?

133
00:13:06,640 --> 00:13:12,770
Tell Lermentov we don't need him to move the tanks.

134
00:13:13,740 --> 00:13:16,350
Tell him he is out.

135
00:13:16,780 --> 00:13:18,400
Well...

136
00:13:21,290 --> 00:13:23,030
...you may have to write it down.

137
00:13:32,010 --> 00:13:33,460
It's for her.

138
00:13:36,930 --> 00:13:38,200
You listen carefully

139
00:13:38,350 --> 00:13:40,910
You're at 1- 14 Silensky Plaza, 3rd floor.

140
00:13:41,180 --> 00:13:43,300
We have an F-22 exactly eight miles out.

141
00:13:44,190 --> 00:13:48,390
Put the woman on the phone, or I will blow up the block before you can make the lobby.

142
00:13:54,870 --> 00:13:55,630
We need you to come in.

143
00:13:55,630 --> 00:13:56,980
Are you kidding? I'm working.

144
00:13:57,200 --> 00:13:58,470
This takes precedence.

145
00:13:58,700 --> 00:14:00,320
I'm in the middle of an interrogation.

146
00:14:00,500 --> 00:14:02,280
This moron is giving me everything.

147
00:14:02,710 --> 00:14:05,330
I don't give everything.

148
00:14:06,760 --> 00:14:08,120
Look, you can't pull me out of this right now.

149
00:14:08,260 --> 00:14:09,250
Natasha...

150
00:14:10,840 --> 00:14:12,330
Barton's been compromised.

151
00:14:15,560 --> 00:14:17,380
Let me put you on hold.

152
00:14:59,150 --> 00:15:00,140
Where is Barton now?

153
00:15:00,320 --> 00:15:01,030
We don't know.

154
00:15:01,030 --> 00:15:02,030
But he's alive?

155
00:15:02,030 --> 00:15:04,810
We think so. I'll brief you on everything when you get back.

156
00:15:05,070 --> 00:15:07,110
But first, we need you to talk to the big guy.

157
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:10,400
Coulson, you know that Stark trusts me about as far as he can throw me.

158
00:15:10,620 --> 00:15:14,110
I've got Stark. You get the big guy.

159
00:15:38,860 --> 00:15:39,850
Who are you?

160
00:15:40,320 --> 00:15:44,010
Get out! There is sickness here!

161
00:15:44,160 --> 00:15:45,150
You're a doctor.

162
00:15:46,870 --> 00:15:48,140
My father's not waking up!

163
00:15:48,290 --> 00:15:51,320
He has a fever and he's moaning but his eyes won't open.

164
00:15:51,460 --> 00:15:52,450
Slow down.

165
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:55,080
My father...

166
00:15:57,470 --> 00:15:58,460
Like them?

167
00:16:02,470 --> 00:16:03,710
Please.

168
00:16:30,920 --> 00:16:33,200
You should've got paid up front, Banner.

169
00:16:33,420 --> 00:16:36,110
You know, for a man who's supposed to be avoiding stress

170
00:16:36,340 --> 00:16:39,590
you picked a hell of a place to settle.

171
00:16:41,350 --> 00:16:43,550
Avoiding stress isn't the secret.

172
00:16:43,770 --> 00:16:46,250
Then what is it? Yoga?

173
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:50,600
You brought me to the edge of the city. Smart.

174
00:16:51,190 --> 00:16:55,230
I assume the whole place is surrounded.

175
00:16:55,700 --> 00:16:57,060
Just you and me.

176
00:16:58,330 --> 00:17:00,360
And your actress buddy?

177
00:17:00,580 --> 00:17:02,530
Is she a spy, too? They start that young?

178
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:04,200
I did.

179
00:17:04,420 --> 00:17:05,440
Who are you?

180
00:17:05,670 --> 00:17:06,770
Natasha Romanoff.

181
00:17:10,130 --> 00:17:11,460
Are you here to kill me, Ms Romanoff?

182
00:17:11,670 --> 00:17:14,380
Because that's not going to work out for everyone.

183
00:17:14,590 --> 00:17:17,050
No, of course not. I'm here on behalf of S.H.I.E.L.D.

184
00:17:18,810 --> 00:17:20,300
S.H.I.E.L.D.

185
00:17:22,100 --> 00:17:23,090
How did they find me?

186
00:17:23,270 --> 00:17:24,890
We never lost you, Doctor.

187
00:17:25,110 --> 00:17:26,100
We've kept our distance.

188
00:17:26,320 --> 00:17:29,300
Even helped keep some other interested parties off your scent.

189
00:17:29,820 --> 00:17:30,810
Why?

190
00:17:30,950 --> 00:17:33,310
Nick Fury seems to trust you.

191
00:17:33,530 --> 00:17:35,150
But now we need you to come in.

192
00:17:36,120 --> 00:17:37,990
What if I say no?

193
00:17:38,210 --> 00:17:40,320
I'll persuade you.

194
00:17:42,460 --> 00:17:46,790
And what if the other guy says no?

195
00:17:47,510 --> 00:17:49,120
You've been more than a year without an incident.

196
00:17:49,340 --> 00:17:51,910
I don't think you want to break that streak.

197
00:17:54,140 --> 00:17:56,760
Well, I don't every time get what I want.

198
00:17:57,810 --> 00:18:00,010
Doctor, we're facing a potential global catastrophe.

199
00:18:00,860 --> 00:18:03,970
Well, those I actively try to avoid.

200
00:18:04,320 --> 00:18:08,940
This is the Tesseract.

201
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:11,940
It has the potential energy to wipe out the planet.

202
00:18:14,790 --> 00:18:16,950
What does Fury want me to do, swallow it?

203
00:18:17,170 --> 00:18:19,620
He wants you to find it. It's been taken.

204
00:18:20,460 --> 00:18:24,620
It emits a gamma signature that's too weak for us to trace.

205
00:18:24,840 --> 00:18:27,750
There's no one that knows gamma radiation like you do.

206
00:18:27,970 --> 00:18:30,750
If there was, that's where I'd be.

207
00:18:31,350 --> 00:18:33,510
So, Fury isn't after the monster?

208
00:18:33,730 --> 00:18:34,970
Not that he's told me.

209
00:18:35,190 --> 00:18:37,350
And he tells you everything?

210
00:18:38,020 --> 00:18:39,390
Talk to Fury. He needs you on this.

211
00:18:39,530 --> 00:18:40,550
He needs me in a cage?

212
00:18:40,690 --> 00:18:41,680
No one's going to put you in a...

213
00:18:41,860 --> 00:18:42,850
Stop lying to me!

214
00:18:47,080 --> 00:18:49,690
I'm sorry. That was mean.

215
00:18:50,660 --> 00:18:52,820
I just wanted to see what you'd do.

216
00:18:54,040 --> 00:18:58,450
Why don't we do this the easy way where you don't use that

217
00:18:58,670 --> 00:19:02,580
and the other guy doesn't make a mess.

218
00:19:03,390 --> 00:19:07,000
Okay? Natasha?

219
00:19:12,690 --> 00:19:13,710
Stand down.

220
00:19:14,690 --> 00:19:16,220
We're good here.

221
00:19:18,070 --> 00:19:19,600
"Just you and me."

222
00:19:21,780 --> 00:19:24,350
This is out of line, Director.

223
00:19:24,580 --> 00:19:26,980
You're dealing with forces you can't control.

224
00:19:27,410 --> 00:19:30,870
You ever been in a war, Councilman? In a firefight?

225
00:19:31,080 --> 00:19:33,870
Did you feel an overabundance of control?

226
00:19:34,090 --> 00:19:37,460
You're saying that this Asgard is declaring war on our planet?

227
00:19:37,590 --> 00:19:40,210
Not Asgard. Loki.

228
00:19:40,430 --> 00:19:43,210
He can't be working alone. What about the other one?

229
00:19:43,350 --> 00:19:44,370
His brother.

230
00:19:44,520 --> 00:19:47,760
Our intelligence says Thor is not a hostile, but he's worlds away.

231
00:19:47,940 --> 00:19:49,720
We can't depend on him to help, either.

232
00:19:49,860 --> 00:19:50,850
It's up to us.

233
00:19:50,980 --> 00:19:53,600
Which is why you should be focusing on Phase 2.

234
00:19:53,780 --> 00:19:55,050
It was designed for exactly this...

235
00:19:55,280 --> 00:19:58,440
Phase 2 isn't ready. Our enemy is.

236
00:19:58,700 --> 00:20:00,230
We need a response team.

237
00:20:00,450 --> 00:20:02,740
The Avengers Initiative was shut down.

238
00:20:02,950 --> 00:20:04,740
This isn't about the Avengers.

239
00:20:04,960 --> 00:20:06,060
We've seen the list.

240
00:20:06,290 --> 00:20:08,490
You're running the world's greatest covert security network

241
00:20:08,630 --> 00:20:11,660
and you're going to leave the fate of the human race to a handful of freaks.

242
00:20:11,800 --> 00:20:13,710
I'm not leaving anything to anyone.

243
00:20:13,920 --> 00:20:16,130
We need a response team.

244
00:20:16,390 --> 00:20:19,090
These people may be isolated, unbalanced even

245
00:20:19,310 --> 00:20:23,470
but I believe with the right push they can be exactly what we need.

246
00:20:23,770 --> 00:20:25,040
You believe?

247
00:20:25,270 --> 00:20:28,850
War isn't won by sentiment, Director.

248
00:20:29,570 --> 00:20:32,890
No, it's won by soldiers.

249
00:20:52,550 --> 00:20:54,340
There's not enough time.

250
00:20:54,550 --> 00:20:56,090
I got to put her in the water!

251
00:21:01,480 --> 00:21:02,500
You won't be alone.

252
00:21:03,110 --> 00:21:04,600
Oh, my God.

253
00:21:05,070 --> 00:21:06,220
This guy is still alive!

254
00:21:31,010 --> 00:21:32,750
Trouble sleeping?

255
00:21:34,100 --> 00:21:36,770
I slept for 70 years, sir. I think I've had my fill.

256
00:21:38,310 --> 00:21:42,220
Then you should be out, celebrating, seeing the world.

257
00:21:48,070 --> 00:21:50,900
When I went under, the world was at war.

258
00:21:51,120 --> 00:21:52,940
I wake up, they say we won.

259
00:21:53,660 --> 00:21:55,200
They didn't say what we lost.

260
00:21:55,790 --> 00:21:58,120
We've made some mistakes along the way.

261
00:21:58,540 --> 00:22:00,200
Some, very recently.

262
00:22:01,760 --> 00:22:02,950
Are you here with a mission, sir?

263
00:22:03,090 --> 00:22:04,080
I am.

264
00:22:04,220 --> 00:22:05,880
Trying to get me back in the world?

265
00:22:06,390 --> 00:22:08,050
Trying to save it.

266
00:22:12,730 --> 00:22:14,720
HYDRA's secret weapon.

267
00:22:14,940 --> 00:22:17,010
Howard Stark fished that out of the ocean

268
00:22:17,150 --> 00:22:18,250
when he was looking for you.

269
00:22:18,820 --> 00:22:20,480
He thought what we think.

270
00:22:20,740 --> 00:22:24,860
The Tesseract could be the key to unlimited sustainable energy.

271
00:22:25,330 --> 00:22:29,150
That's something the world sorely needs.

272
00:22:30,660 --> 00:22:31,820
Who took it from you?

273
00:22:32,040 --> 00:22:33,450
He's called Loki.

274
00:22:33,670 --> 00:22:36,290
He's not from around here.

275
00:22:36,750 --> 00:22:40,150
There's a lot we'll have to bring you up to speed on if you're in.

276
00:22:41,090 --> 00:22:44,340
The world has gotten even stranger than you already know.

277
00:22:44,850 --> 00:22:47,410
At this point, I doubt anything would surprise me.

278
00:22:48,060 --> 00:22:49,720
Ten bucks says you're wrong.

279
00:22:51,480 --> 00:22:55,350
There's a debriefing packet waiting for you back at your apartment.

280
00:22:57,740 --> 00:23:00,970
Is there anything you can tell us about the Tesseract that we ought to know now?

281
00:23:01,280 --> 00:23:03,570
You should have left it in the ocean.

282
00:23:36,320 --> 00:23:39,190
Good to go on this end. The rest is up to you.

283
00:23:39,410 --> 00:23:40,730
You disconnected the transmission lines?

284
00:23:40,870 --> 00:23:41,860
Are we off the grid?

285
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:45,780
Stark Tower is about to become a beacon of self-sustaining clean energy.

286
00:23:45,920 --> 00:23:49,280
Well, assuming the arc reactor takes over and it actually works.

287
00:23:49,670 --> 00:23:50,940
I assume.

288
00:23:51,470 --> 00:23:52,460
Light her up.

289
00:23:58,010 --> 00:23:59,010
How does it look?

290
00:23:59,180 --> 00:24:01,850
Like Christmas, but with more me.

291
00:24:02,060 --> 00:24:03,800
We've got to go wider on the public awareness campaign.

292
00:24:04,020 --> 00:24:05,040
You need to do some press.

293
00:24:05,690 --> 00:24:08,350
I'm in DC tomorrow, I'm working on the zoning for the next three buildings.

294
00:24:08,530 --> 00:24:10,730
Pepper, you're killing me. The moment, remember?

295
00:24:10,950 --> 00:24:11,970
Enjoy the moment.

296
00:24:12,200 --> 00:24:13,360
Get in here and I will.

297
00:24:16,700 --> 00:24:19,610
Sir, Agent Coulson of S.H.I.E.L.D. Is on the line.

298
00:24:20,210 --> 00:24:21,200
I'm not in.

299
00:24:21,880 --> 00:24:23,150
I'm actually out.

300
00:24:30,380 --> 00:24:33,000
Sir, I'm afraid he's insisting.

301
00:24:33,220 --> 00:24:35,960
Grow a spine, Jarvis. I got a date.

302
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:43,470
Levels are holding steady, I think.

303
00:24:43,690 --> 00:24:45,850
Of course they are. I was directly involved.

304
00:24:46,070 --> 00:24:47,230
Which brings me to my next question.

305
00:24:47,400 --> 00:24:49,350
How does it feel to be a genius?

306
00:24:49,570 --> 00:24:51,820
Well, I really wouldn't know, now would I?

307
00:24:52,030 --> 00:24:56,530
What do you mean? All this came from you.

308
00:24:56,750 --> 00:25:00,370
No, all this came from that.

309
00:25:00,590 --> 00:25:02,870
Give yourself some credit. Please.

310
00:25:03,090 --> 00:25:04,870
Stark Tower is your baby.

311
00:25:05,090 --> 00:25:07,460
Give yourself 12% of the credit.

312
00:25:07,930 --> 00:25:09,030
12%?

313
00:25:09,180 --> 00:25:10,280
An argument can be made for 15.

314
00:25:10,430 --> 00:25:12,010
12%? My baby?

315
00:25:12,220 --> 00:25:13,800
Well, I did do all the heavy lifting.

316
00:25:13,930 --> 00:25:15,800
Literally, I lifted the heavy things.

317
00:25:16,060 --> 00:25:19,890
And, sorry, but the security snafu? That was on you.

318
00:25:20,070 --> 00:25:20,790
My private elevator...

319
00:25:20,790 --> 00:25:22,140
You mean our elevator?

320
00:25:22,360 --> 00:25:25,030
...it was teeming with sweaty workmen.

321
00:25:25,240 --> 00:25:29,730
I'm going to pay for that comment about percentages in some subtle way later, aren't I?

322
00:25:30,200 --> 00:25:31,390
It's not going to be that subtle.

323
00:25:31,620 --> 00:25:32,890
I'll tell you what.

324
00:25:33,120 --> 00:25:35,570
The next building is gonna say "Potts" on the tower.

325
00:25:35,790 --> 00:25:37,160
On the lease.

326
00:25:38,090 --> 00:25:40,200
Call your mom. Can you bunk over?

327
00:25:40,420 --> 00:25:41,660
Sir, the telephone.

328
00:25:41,880 --> 00:25:44,250
I'm afraid my protocols are being overridden.

329
00:25:44,470 --> 00:25:46,420
Mr Stark, we need to talk.

330
00:25:46,720 --> 00:25:50,220
You have reached the life model decoy of Tony Stark. Please leave a message.

331
00:25:50,220 --> 00:25:51,260
This is urgent.

332
00:25:51,480 --> 00:25:52,840
Then leave it urgently.

333
00:25:54,810 --> 00:25:55,920
Security breach. It's on you.

334
00:25:56,050 --> 00:25:56,620
Mr Stark.

335
00:25:56,620 --> 00:25:58,850
Phil! Come in.

336
00:25:59,030 --> 00:26:00,020
"Phil"?

337
00:26:00,150 --> 00:26:01,180
I can't stay.

338
00:26:01,410 --> 00:26:02,590
His first name is "Agent."

339
00:26:02,820 --> 00:26:04,440
Come on in. We're celebrating.

340
00:26:04,660 --> 00:26:06,440
Which is why he can't stay.

341
00:26:06,660 --> 00:26:08,610
We need you to look this over as soon as possible.

342
00:26:08,830 --> 00:26:09,850
I don't like being handed things.

343
00:26:10,080 --> 00:26:11,530
That's fine, because I love to be handed things.

344
00:26:11,750 --> 00:26:13,080
So, let's trade.

345
00:26:14,460 --> 00:26:15,950
Thank you.

346
00:26:17,170 --> 00:26:20,500
Official consulting hours are between 8 and 5 every other Thursday.

347
00:26:20,680 --> 00:26:21,670
This isn't a consultation.

348
00:26:21,800 --> 00:26:23,050
Is this about the Avengers?

349
00:26:23,470 --> 00:26:25,170
Which I know nothing about.

350
00:26:25,170 --> 00:26:27,990
The Avengers Initiative was scrapped, I thought.

351
00:26:27,990 --> 00:26:29,480
And I didn't even qualify.

352
00:26:29,480 --> 00:26:30,550
I didn't know that either.

353
00:26:30,550 --> 00:26:34,900
Apparently I'm volatile, self-obsessed, don't play well with others.

354
00:26:35,410 --> 00:26:36,360
That I did know.

355
00:26:36,360 --> 00:26:38,120
This isn't about personality profiles any more.

356
00:26:38,120 --> 00:26:40,710
Whatever. Ms Potts, got a second?

357
00:26:40,710 --> 00:26:41,590
Half a mo.

358
00:26:47,070 --> 00:26:49,610
You know, I thought we were having a moment.

359
00:26:49,610 --> 00:26:51,230
I was having 12% of a moment.

360
00:26:52,440 --> 00:26:55,100
This seems serious. Phil's pretty shaken.

361
00:26:55,100 --> 00:26:57,290
How would you know if it's... Why is he "Phil"?

362
00:26:57,290 --> 00:26:58,360
What is all this?

363
00:26:59,230 --> 00:26:59,990
This is

364
00:27:01,360 --> 00:27:02,150
this.

365
00:27:09,920 --> 00:27:11,740
I'm going to take the jet to DC tonight.

366
00:27:11,740 --> 00:27:12,500
Tomorrow.

367
00:27:12,500 --> 00:27:15,100
You have homework. You have a lot of homework.

368
00:27:15,100 --> 00:27:16,720
Well, what if I didn't?

369
00:27:17,350 --> 00:27:18,110
If you didn't?

370
00:27:18,110 --> 00:27:18,750
Yeah.

371
00:27:18,940 --> 00:27:20,560
You mean when you've finished?

372
00:27:22,420 --> 00:27:25,780
Well, then...

373
00:27:30,720 --> 00:27:32,180
Square deal. Fly safe.

374
00:27:36,340 --> 00:27:37,320
Work hard.

375
00:27:40,130 --> 00:27:42,090
So, any chance you're driving by LaGuardia?

376
00:27:42,090 --> 00:27:42,800
I can drop you.

377
00:27:43,350 --> 00:27:44,480
Fantastic.

378
00:27:45,060 --> 00:27:47,930
I want to hear about the cellist. Is that still a thing?

379
00:27:47,930 --> 00:27:49,310
She moved back to Portland.

380
00:27:49,310 --> 00:27:51,800
What? Boo!

381
00:28:00,490 --> 00:28:02,520
We're about 40 minutes out from home base, sir.

382
00:28:06,720 --> 00:28:10,270
So, this Dr Banner was trying to replicate the serum they used on me?

383
00:28:10,630 --> 00:28:11,940
A lot of people were.

384
00:28:12,280 --> 00:28:13,870
You were the world's first superhero.

385
00:28:14,680 --> 00:28:18,610
Banner thought gamma radiation might hold the key to unlocking Erskine's original formula.

386
00:28:19,930 --> 00:28:21,400
Didn't really go his way, did it?

387
00:28:21,400 --> 00:28:22,550
Not so much.

388
00:28:23,330 --> 00:28:26,120
When he's not that thing, though, the guy's like a Stephen Hawking.

389
00:28:28,330 --> 00:28:30,350
He's like a smart person.

390
00:28:32,890 --> 00:28:33,680
I gotta say,

391
00:28:34,330 --> 00:28:36,860
it's an honour to meet you officially.

392
00:28:37,590 --> 00:28:40,970
I've sort of met you. I mean, I watched you while you were sleeping.

393
00:28:42,760 --> 00:28:48,600
I mean, I was present while you were unconscious from the ice.

394
00:28:48,600 --> 00:28:52,600
You know, it's really just a huge honour to have you on board this...

395
00:28:53,750 --> 00:28:54,980
I hope I'm the man for the job.

396
00:28:55,530 --> 00:28:57,830
Oh, you are. Absolutely.

397
00:28:58,630 --> 00:29:01,140
We made some modifications to the uniform.

398
00:29:01,870 --> 00:29:03,510
I had a little design input.

399
00:29:03,510 --> 00:29:04,460
The uniform?

400
00:29:04,900 --> 00:29:06,880
Aren't the stars and stripes a little

401
00:29:08,670 --> 00:29:09,610
old-fashioned?

402
00:29:10,780 --> 00:29:12,290
With everything that's happening

403
00:29:13,200 --> 00:29:15,020
and the things that are about to come to light,

404
00:29:15,750 --> 00:29:18,920
people might just need a little old-fashioned.

405
00:29:51,960 --> 00:29:54,720
The Chitauri grow restless.

406
00:29:54,720 --> 00:29:56,480
Let them gird themselves.

407
00:29:56,480 --> 00:29:58,420
I will lead them in the glorious battle.

408
00:29:58,670 --> 00:29:59,820
Battle?

409
00:30:00,700 --> 00:30:03,960
Against the meagre might of Earth?

410
00:30:03,960 --> 00:30:06,510
Glorious, not lengthy.

411
00:30:07,030 --> 00:30:11,000
If your force is as formidable as you claim.

412
00:30:11,000 --> 00:30:12,940
You question us?

413
00:30:13,750 --> 00:30:15,380
You question him,

414
00:30:15,850 --> 00:30:18,480
he who put the sceptre in your hand?

415
00:30:18,480 --> 00:30:24,890
Who gave you ancient knowledge and new purpose when you were cast out, defeated?

416
00:30:24,890 --> 00:30:26,410
I was a king!

417
00:30:26,890 --> 00:30:28,680
The rightful king of Asgard,

418
00:30:29,700 --> 00:30:30,820
betrayed.

419
00:30:31,340 --> 00:30:33,990
Your ambition is little

420
00:30:34,460 --> 00:30:36,820
and born of childish need.

421
00:30:37,220 --> 00:30:42,870
We look beyond the Earth to the greater worlds the Tesseract will unveil.

422
00:30:42,870 --> 00:30:44,360
You don't have the Tesseract yet.

423
00:30:46,970 --> 00:30:48,300
I don't threaten.

424
00:30:49,610 --> 00:30:51,420
But until I open the doors,

425
00:30:52,320 --> 00:30:55,480
until your force is mine to command,

426
00:30:56,810 --> 00:30:58,580
you are but words.

427
00:30:58,580 --> 00:31:02,680
You will have your war, Asgardian.

428
00:31:04,750 --> 00:31:06,740
If you fail,

429
00:31:07,760 --> 00:31:11,770
if the Tesseract is kept from us,

430
00:31:12,170 --> 00:31:16,220
there will be no realm, no barren moon,

431
00:31:16,740 --> 00:31:20,030
no crevice where he cannot find you.

432
00:31:21,670 --> 00:31:24,490
You think you know pain?

433
00:31:24,490 --> 00:31:30,050
He will make you long for something sweet as pain.

434
00:31:59,410 --> 00:32:00,210
Stow the captain's gear.

435
00:32:00,210 --> 00:32:00,850
Yes, sir.

436
00:32:03,120 --> 00:32:06,070
Agent Romanoff, Captain Rogers.

437
00:32:06,480 --> 00:32:07,040
Ma'am.

438
00:32:07,040 --> 00:32:07,880
Hi.

439
00:32:07,880 --> 00:32:10,400
They need you on the bridge. They're starting the face-trace.

440
00:32:10,620 --> 00:32:11,510
See you there.

441
00:32:13,600 --> 00:32:17,000
It was quite the buzz around here, finding you in the ice.

442
00:32:17,980 --> 00:32:19,880
I thought Coulson was gonna swoon.

443
00:32:20,790 --> 00:32:23,530
Did he ask you to sign his Captain America trading cards yet?

444
00:32:23,930 --> 00:32:24,830
Trading cards?

445
00:32:25,250 --> 00:32:27,310
They're vintage. He's very proud.

446
00:32:29,130 --> 00:32:30,260
Dr Banner.

447
00:32:31,930 --> 00:32:35,690
Yeah, hi. They told me you would be coming.

448
00:32:35,690 --> 00:32:37,090
Word is, you can find the Cube.

449
00:32:38,130 --> 00:32:40,080
Is that the only word on me?

450
00:32:40,080 --> 00:32:41,540
Only word I care about.

451
00:32:44,050 --> 00:32:46,670
It must be strange for you, all of this.

452
00:32:47,410 --> 00:32:50,050
Well, this is actually kind of familiar.

453
00:32:50,050 --> 00:32:52,930
Gentlemen, you might want to step inside in a minute.

454
00:32:52,930 --> 00:32:55,250
It's going to get a little hard to breathe.

455
00:32:57,010 --> 00:32:58,650
Flight crew, secure the deck.

456
00:33:03,140 --> 00:33:04,670
Is this a submarine?

457
00:33:05,320 --> 00:33:06,160
Really?

458
00:33:06,160 --> 00:33:09,700
They want me in a submerged, pressurised, metal container?

459
00:33:36,580 --> 00:33:38,340
No, no, this is much worse.

460
00:34:09,090 --> 00:34:11,710
Hover power check complete. Position cyclic.

461
00:34:19,230 --> 00:34:23,110
Preparing for maximum performance takeoff. Increase output to capacity.

462
00:34:23,110 --> 00:34:26,920
Power plant performing at capacity. We are clear.

463
00:34:27,350 --> 00:34:28,950
All engines operating.

464
00:34:28,950 --> 00:34:33,500
S.H.I.E.L.D. Emergency Protocol 193.6 in effect.

465
00:34:33,830 --> 00:34:35,170
We are at level, sir.

466
00:34:35,170 --> 00:34:36,100
Good.

467
00:34:36,850 --> 00:34:38,040
Let's vanish.

468
00:34:38,040 --> 00:34:40,100
Engage retro-reflection panels.

469
00:34:56,220 --> 00:34:57,550
Reflection panels engaged.

470
00:34:57,820 --> 00:34:58,780
Gentlemen.

471
00:35:11,620 --> 00:35:12,980
Doctor, thank you for coming.

472
00:35:14,790 --> 00:35:16,600
Thanks for asking nicely.

473
00:35:16,910 --> 00:35:19,640
So, how long am I staying?

474
00:35:19,640 --> 00:35:22,660
Once we get our hands on the Tesseract, you're in the wind.

475
00:35:22,660 --> 00:35:24,280
Where are you with that?

476
00:35:24,940 --> 00:35:28,140
We're sweeping every wirelessly accessible camera on the planet.

477
00:35:28,530 --> 00:35:30,340
Cell phones, laptops...

478
00:35:30,960 --> 00:35:33,890
If it's connected to a satellite, it's eyes and ears for us.

479
00:35:33,890 --> 00:35:35,590
That's still not gonna find them in time.

480
00:35:35,590 --> 00:35:36,900
You have to narrow your field.

481
00:35:36,900 --> 00:35:38,860
How many spectrometers do you have access to?

482
00:35:38,860 --> 00:35:39,820
How many are there?

483
00:35:39,820 --> 00:35:42,630
Call every lab you know. Tell them to put the spectrometers on the roof

484
00:35:42,630 --> 00:35:44,480
and calibrate them for gamma rays.

485
00:35:44,480 --> 00:35:47,770
I'll rough out a tracking algorithm, basic cluster recognition.

486
00:35:47,770 --> 00:35:50,250
At least we could rule out a few places.

487
00:35:50,780 --> 00:35:52,040
Do you have somewhere for me to work?

488
00:35:52,690 --> 00:35:55,790
Agent Romanoff, could you show Dr Banner to his laboratory, please?

489
00:35:57,500 --> 00:35:59,500
You're gonna love it, Doc. We got all the toys.

490
00:36:00,300 --> 00:36:01,810
Put it over there.

491
00:36:04,150 --> 00:36:05,820
Where did you find all these people?

492
00:36:06,360 --> 00:36:08,900
S.H.I.E.L.D. Has no shortage of enemies, Doctor.

493
00:36:09,810 --> 00:36:11,080
Is this the stuff you need?

494
00:36:11,080 --> 00:36:12,110
Yeah, iridium.

495
00:36:12,110 --> 00:36:14,740
It's found in meteorites. It forms anti-protons.

496
00:36:15,030 --> 00:36:16,560
It's very hard to get hold of.

497
00:36:17,040 --> 00:36:18,690
Especially if S.H.I.E.L.D. Knows you need it.

498
00:36:18,690 --> 00:36:19,980
Well, I didn't know.

499
00:36:20,320 --> 00:36:23,970
Hey! The Tesseract has shown me so much.

500
00:36:24,370 --> 00:36:26,580
It's more than knowledge. It's truth.

501
00:36:26,580 --> 00:36:27,400
I know.

502
00:36:28,270 --> 00:36:29,960
What did it show you, Agent Barton?

503
00:36:31,150 --> 00:36:32,350
My next target.

504
00:36:32,710 --> 00:36:34,120
Tell me what you need.

505
00:36:37,340 --> 00:36:38,580
I need a distraction.

506
00:36:39,920 --> 00:36:41,130
And an eyeball.

507
00:36:48,120 --> 00:36:50,670
I mean, if it's not too much trouble.

508
00:36:50,670 --> 00:36:52,220
No, no. It's fine.

509
00:36:54,960 --> 00:36:56,320
It's a vintage set.

510
00:36:56,880 --> 00:36:58,830
It took me a couple of years to collect them all.

511
00:37:01,710 --> 00:37:02,990
Near mint.

512
00:37:02,990 --> 00:37:04,730
Slight foxing around the edges, but...

513
00:37:04,730 --> 00:37:07,410
We got a hit. A 67% match.

514
00:37:07,410 --> 00:37:09,530
Wait. Cross match, 79%.

515
00:37:10,470 --> 00:37:11,300
Location?

516
00:37:11,300 --> 00:37:14,620
Stuttgart, Germany. 28 Konigstrabe.

517
00:37:14,620 --> 00:37:15,900
He's not exactly hiding.

518
00:37:15,900 --> 00:37:16,830
Captain,

519
00:37:17,890 --> 00:37:18,880
you're up.

520
00:39:54,190 --> 00:39:55,420
Kneel before me.

521
00:39:59,780 --> 00:40:00,860
I said

522
00:40:03,240 --> 00:40:05,390
kneel!

523
00:40:14,770 --> 00:40:17,730
Is not this simpler?

524
00:40:19,610 --> 00:40:22,740
Is this not your natural state?

525
00:40:25,060 --> 00:40:27,940
It's the unspoken truth of humanity,

526
00:40:28,440 --> 00:40:30,840
that you crave subjugation.

527
00:40:31,500 --> 00:40:35,500
The bright lure of freedom diminishes your life's joy

528
00:40:35,500 --> 00:40:38,650
in a mad scramble for power,

529
00:40:39,990 --> 00:40:41,380
for identity.

530
00:40:42,850 --> 00:40:46,460
You were made to be ruled.

531
00:40:46,900 --> 00:40:48,240
In the end,

532
00:40:48,760 --> 00:40:50,810
you will always kneel.

533
00:40:58,390 --> 00:41:00,210
Not to men like you.

534
00:41:01,490 --> 00:41:03,370
There are no men like me.

535
00:41:04,260 --> 00:41:07,180
There are always men like you.

536
00:41:08,410 --> 00:41:10,390
Look to your elder, people.

537
00:41:12,460 --> 00:41:14,340
Let him be an example.

538
00:41:20,730 --> 00:41:22,860
You know, the last time I was in Germany,

539
00:41:23,470 --> 00:41:26,050
and saw a man standing above everybody else,

540
00:41:26,870 --> 00:41:28,430
we ended up disagreeing.

541
00:41:28,430 --> 00:41:30,110
The soldier.

542
00:41:32,640 --> 00:41:33,890
The man out of time.

543
00:41:34,430 --> 00:41:35,460
I'm not the one who's out of time.

544
00:41:39,340 --> 00:41:41,730
Loki, drop the weapon and stand down.

545
00:42:01,920 --> 00:42:02,880
Kneel.

546
00:42:03,900 --> 00:42:04,750
Not today!

547
00:42:07,310 --> 00:42:08,520
The guy's all over the place.

548
00:42:11,830 --> 00:42:14,250
Agent Romanoff. You miss me?

549
00:42:31,230 --> 00:42:33,140
Make your move, Reindeer Games.

550
00:42:41,110 --> 00:42:42,020
Good move.

551
00:42:44,240 --> 00:42:45,210
Mr Stark.

552
00:42:45,930 --> 00:42:46,710
Captain.

553
00:42:54,610 --> 00:42:55,990
Is he saying anything?

554
00:42:56,400 --> 00:42:57,490
Not a word.

555
00:42:58,000 --> 00:42:59,900
Just get him here. We're low on time.

556
00:43:03,180 --> 00:43:04,050
I don't like it.

557
00:43:04,050 --> 00:43:06,300
What, Rock of Ages giving up so easily?

558
00:43:06,300 --> 00:43:07,920
I don't remember it being that easy.

559
00:43:08,460 --> 00:43:09,780
This guy packs a wallop.

560
00:43:09,780 --> 00:43:12,730
Still, you are pretty spry for an older fellow.

561
00:43:14,560 --> 00:43:15,880
What's your thing, Pilates?

562
00:43:16,430 --> 00:43:17,100
What?

563
00:43:17,100 --> 00:43:18,380
It's like calisthenics.

564
00:43:18,380 --> 00:43:20,030
You might have missed a couple of things

565
00:43:20,800 --> 00:43:22,430
doing time as a Capsicle.

566
00:43:24,480 --> 00:43:26,140
Fury didn't tell me he was calling you in.

567
00:43:26,140 --> 00:43:28,070
Yeah, there's a lot of things Fury doesn't tell you.

568
00:43:29,380 --> 00:43:30,240
Where's this coming from?

569
00:43:35,130 --> 00:43:37,540
What's the matter? Are you scared of a little lightning?

570
00:43:38,070 --> 00:43:40,350
I'm not overly fond of what follows.

571
00:43:58,260 --> 00:43:59,110
What are you doing?

572
00:44:12,570 --> 00:44:13,780
And now there's that guy.

573
00:44:13,780 --> 00:44:15,230
Another Asgardian?

574
00:44:15,950 --> 00:44:16,930
That guy's a friendly?

575
00:44:16,930 --> 00:44:17,690
Doesn't matter.

576
00:44:17,690 --> 00:44:20,570
If he frees Loki or kills him, the Tesseract's lost.

577
00:44:20,570 --> 00:44:22,730
Stark, we need a plan of attack!

578
00:44:22,730 --> 00:44:24,940
I have a plan. Attack.

579
00:44:31,200 --> 00:44:32,440
I'd sit this one out, Cap.

580
00:44:33,230 --> 00:44:34,250
I don't see how I can.

581
00:44:34,250 --> 00:44:36,510
These guys come from legend. They're basically gods.

582
00:44:37,420 --> 00:44:38,910
There's only one God, ma'am.

583
00:44:39,040 --> 00:44:40,720
And I'm pretty sure he doesn't dress like that.

584
00:44:56,660 --> 00:44:57,910
Where is the Tesseract?

585
00:44:58,480 --> 00:44:59,790
I missed you, too.

586
00:44:59,790 --> 00:45:01,380
Do I look to be in a gaming mood?

587
00:45:02,110 --> 00:45:03,310
You should thank me.

588
00:45:04,280 --> 00:45:08,850
With the Bifrost gone, how much dark energy did the Allfather have to  to conjure you here

589
00:45:09,430 --> 00:45:10,580
to your precious Earth?

590
00:45:14,810 --> 00:45:16,040
I thought you dead.

591
00:45:17,540 --> 00:45:18,730
Did you mourn?

592
00:45:19,520 --> 00:45:21,610
We all did. Our father...

593
00:45:21,610 --> 00:45:24,360
Your father.

594
00:45:26,420 --> 00:45:28,650
He did tell you my true parentage, did he not?

595
00:45:31,820 --> 00:45:33,490
We were raised together.

596
00:45:34,290 --> 00:45:36,740
We played together, we fought together.

597
00:45:37,510 --> 00:45:38,850
Do you remember none of that?

598
00:45:38,850 --> 00:45:40,380
I remember a shadow.

599
00:45:42,260 --> 00:45:44,840
Living in the shade of your greatness.

600
00:45:46,010 --> 00:45:48,870
I remember you tossing me into an abyss.

601
00:45:48,870 --> 00:45:51,000
I, who was, and should be, king!

602
00:45:51,000 --> 00:45:54,700
So you take the world I love as a recompense for your imagined slights?

603
00:45:55,520 --> 00:45:58,150
No. The Earth is under my protection, Loki.

604
00:45:59,910 --> 00:46:03,260
And you're doing a marvellous job with that.

605
00:46:03,770 --> 00:46:05,890
The humans slaughter each other in droves

606
00:46:05,890 --> 00:46:07,540
while you idly fret.

607
00:46:07,970 --> 00:46:10,240
I mean to rule them, as why should I not?

608
00:46:10,240 --> 00:46:11,900
You think yourself above them?

609
00:46:12,990 --> 00:46:13,940
Well, yes.

610
00:46:13,940 --> 00:46:16,550
Then you miss the truth of ruling, brother.

611
00:46:17,520 --> 00:46:18,950
A throne would suit you ill.

612
00:46:24,050 --> 00:46:26,430
I've seen worlds you've never known about!

613
00:46:26,830 --> 00:46:30,930
I have grown, Odinson, in my exile.

614
00:46:31,500 --> 00:46:33,710
I have seen the true power of the Tesseract,

615
00:46:33,710 --> 00:46:34,680
and when I wield it...

616
00:46:34,680 --> 00:46:36,300
Who showed you this power?

617
00:46:37,810 --> 00:46:39,270
Who controls the would-be king?

618
00:46:39,270 --> 00:46:40,010
I am a king!

619
00:46:40,010 --> 00:46:41,370
Not here!

620
00:46:41,370 --> 00:46:42,650
You give up the Tesseract!

621
00:46:42,650 --> 00:46:44,600
You give up this poisonous dream!

622
00:46:48,130 --> 00:46:49,470
You come home.

623
00:46:54,400 --> 00:46:55,530
I don't have it.

624
00:46:57,510 --> 00:46:59,440
You need the Cube to bring me home.

625
00:46:59,440 --> 00:47:01,630
But I've sent it off, I know not where.

626
00:47:02,920 --> 00:47:04,600
You listen well, brother.

627
00:47:06,750 --> 00:47:07,620
I'm listening.

628
00:47:17,110 --> 00:47:18,610
Do not touch me again.

629
00:47:18,900 --> 00:47:20,170
Then don't take my stuff.

630
00:47:20,720 --> 00:47:22,970
You have no idea what you're dealing with.

631
00:47:24,850 --> 00:47:25,770
Shakespeare in the Park?

632
00:47:26,950 --> 00:47:30,120
Doth Mother know you wear-eth her drapes?

633
00:47:30,660 --> 00:47:32,900
This is beyond you, metal man.

634
00:47:33,620 --> 00:47:35,890
Loki will face Asgardian justice.

635
00:47:35,890 --> 00:47:38,560
He gives up the Cube, he's all yours. Until then,

636
00:47:39,580 --> 00:47:40,410
stay out of the way.

637
00:47:42,390 --> 00:47:43,100
Tourist.

638
00:47:49,520 --> 00:47:50,370
Okay.

639
00:48:20,450 --> 00:48:23,040
Power at 400% capacity.

640
00:48:23,530 --> 00:48:24,440
How about that?

641
00:49:25,090 --> 00:49:25,650
Hey!

642
00:49:29,080 --> 00:49:30,140
That's enough.

643
00:49:34,280 --> 00:49:35,750
Now, I don't know what you plan on doing here.

644
00:49:35,750 --> 00:49:38,350
I've come here to put an end to Loki's schemes.

645
00:49:38,350 --> 00:49:40,980
Then prove it. Put that hammer down.

646
00:49:41,320 --> 00:49:42,230
Yeah... No.

647
00:49:42,230 --> 00:49:43,940
Bad call. He loves his hammer.

648
00:49:45,580 --> 00:49:47,030
You want me to put the hammer down?

649
00:50:15,160 --> 00:50:16,250
Are we done, here?

650
00:51:04,710 --> 00:51:06,290
In case it's unclear,

651
00:51:08,490 --> 00:51:09,650
if you try to escape,

652
00:51:11,390 --> 00:51:13,510
if you so much as scratch that glass,

653
00:51:23,190 --> 00:51:27,240
it's 30,000 feet straight down in a steel trap.

654
00:51:27,720 --> 00:51:29,120
You get how that works?

655
00:51:31,850 --> 00:51:34,270
Ant, boot.

656
00:51:37,820 --> 00:51:39,430
It's an impressive cage.

657
00:51:40,470 --> 00:51:42,710
Not built, I think, for me.

658
00:51:43,470 --> 00:51:46,020
Built for something a lot stronger than you.

659
00:51:46,020 --> 00:51:47,350
Oh, I've heard.

660
00:51:49,090 --> 00:51:50,440
A mindless beast.

661
00:51:51,260 --> 00:51:53,060
Makes play he's still a man.

662
00:51:53,980 --> 00:51:56,000
How desperate are you,

663
00:51:56,410 --> 00:51:59,330
that you call on such lost creatures to defend you?

664
00:51:59,760 --> 00:52:01,870
How desperate am I?

665
00:52:02,490 --> 00:52:04,140
You threaten my world with war.

666
00:52:04,140 --> 00:52:06,520
You steal a force you can't hope to control.

667
00:52:06,520 --> 00:52:10,050
You talk about peace, and you kill because it's fun.

668
00:52:10,600 --> 00:52:13,380
You have made me very desperate.

669
00:52:13,840 --> 00:52:15,600
You might not be glad that you did.

670
00:52:19,000 --> 00:52:21,720
It burns you to have come so close.

671
00:52:23,660 --> 00:52:26,500
To have the Tesseract, to have power,

672
00:52:27,230 --> 00:52:29,040
unlimited power.

673
00:52:29,850 --> 00:52:31,370
And for what?

674
00:52:33,290 --> 00:52:35,830
A warm light for all mankind to share.

675
00:52:37,340 --> 00:52:40,410
And then to be reminded what real power is.

676
00:52:44,590 --> 00:52:48,570
Well, let me know if "real power" wants a magazine or something.

677
00:52:57,410 --> 00:52:58,830
He really grows on you, doesn't he?

678
00:52:58,830 --> 00:53:00,250
Loki's gonna drag this out.

679
00:53:01,000 --> 00:53:04,530
So, Thor, what's his play?

680
00:53:04,530 --> 00:53:07,000
He has an army called the Chitauri.

681
00:53:07,590 --> 00:53:09,960
They're not of Asgard, nor any world known.

682
00:53:11,170 --> 00:53:13,000
He means to lead them against your people.

683
00:53:13,000 --> 00:53:14,520
They will win him the Earth,

684
00:53:15,000 --> 00:53:16,760
in return, I suspect, for the Tesseract.

685
00:53:16,760 --> 00:53:17,830
An army

686
00:53:18,790 --> 00:53:19,990
from outer space.

687
00:53:20,640 --> 00:53:22,420
So, he's building another portal.

688
00:53:23,280 --> 00:53:25,080
That's what he needs Erik Selvig for.

689
00:53:25,080 --> 00:53:25,690
Selvig?

690
00:53:26,080 --> 00:53:27,470
He's an astrophysicist.

691
00:53:27,470 --> 00:53:28,390
He's a friend.

692
00:53:28,390 --> 00:53:30,580
Loki has him under some kind of spell,

693
00:53:31,420 --> 00:53:32,470
along with one of ours.

694
00:53:32,470 --> 00:53:34,040
I want to know why Loki let us take him.

695
00:53:34,380 --> 00:53:35,600
He's not leading an army from here.

696
00:53:35,600 --> 00:53:37,530
I don't think we should be focusing on Loki.

697
00:53:37,530 --> 00:53:39,550
That guy's brain is a bag full of cats.

698
00:53:39,550 --> 00:53:40,920
You could smell crazy on him.

699
00:53:40,920 --> 00:53:42,460
Have care how you speak.

700
00:53:43,320 --> 00:53:45,450
Loki is beyond reason, but he is of Asgard.

701
00:53:45,970 --> 00:53:46,860
And he is my brother.

702
00:53:47,370 --> 00:53:49,180
He killed 80 people in two days.

703
00:53:49,910 --> 00:53:50,960
He's adopted.

704
00:53:50,960 --> 00:53:53,040
I think it's about the mechanics.

705
00:53:53,650 --> 00:53:55,790
Iridium... What do they need the iridium for?

706
00:53:55,790 --> 00:53:56,700
It's a stabilising agent.

707
00:53:57,170 --> 00:53:58,380
I'm just saying, pick a weekend.

708
00:53:58,380 --> 00:53:59,470
I'll fly you to Portland.

709
00:53:59,990 --> 00:54:00,910
Keep love alive.

710
00:54:01,870 --> 00:54:04,820
It means the portal won't collapse on itself like it did at S.H.I.E.L.D.

711
00:54:06,080 --> 00:54:08,450
No hard feelings, Point Break. You've got a mean swing.

712
00:54:09,490 --> 00:54:11,850
Also, it means the portal can open as wide

713
00:54:11,850 --> 00:54:14,150
and stay open as long, as Loki wants.

714
00:54:15,270 --> 00:54:17,240
Raise the mizzenmast. Jib the topsails.

715
00:54:18,810 --> 00:54:20,410
That man is playing Galaga.

716
00:54:21,290 --> 00:54:24,060
He thought we wouldn't notice, but we did.

717
00:54:26,570 --> 00:54:28,030
How does Fury even see these?

718
00:54:28,450 --> 00:54:29,060
He turns.

719
00:54:29,370 --> 00:54:30,650
Sounds exhausting.

720
00:54:32,100 --> 00:54:36,090
The rest of the raw materials, Agent Barton can get his hands on pretty easily.

721
00:54:36,580 --> 00:54:41,580
The only major component he still needs is a power source of high-energy density.

722
00:54:41,580 --> 00:54:44,960
Something to kick-start the Cube.

723
00:54:45,260 --> 00:54:48,140
When did you become an expert in thermonuclear astrophysics?

724
00:54:48,520 --> 00:54:49,200
Last night.

725
00:54:50,170 --> 00:54:53,220
The packet, Selvig's notes, the extraction theory papers.

726
00:54:53,220 --> 00:54:54,620
Am I the only one who did the reading?

727
00:54:54,620 --> 00:54:56,850
Does Loki need any particular kind of power source?

728
00:54:57,420 --> 00:55:00,330
He would have to heat the Cube to 120-million Kelvin

729
00:55:00,330 --> 00:55:02,050
just to break through the Coulomb barrier.

730
00:55:02,050 --> 00:55:05,840
Unless Selvig has figured out how to stabilise the quantum tunnelling effect.

731
00:55:05,840 --> 00:55:06,780
Well, if he could do that,

732
00:55:06,780 --> 00:55:09,750
he could achieve heavy ion fusion at any reactor on the planet.

733
00:55:09,750 --> 00:55:11,630
Finally, someone who speaks English.

734
00:55:12,580 --> 00:55:13,610
Is that what just happened?

735
00:55:14,450 --> 00:55:15,800
It's good to meet you, Dr Banner.

736
00:55:16,740 --> 00:55:19,620
Your work on antielectron collisions is unparalleled.

737
00:55:20,000 --> 00:55:21,980
And I'm a huge fan of the way you lose control

738
00:55:21,980 --> 00:55:23,930
and turn into an enormous green rage-monster.

739
00:55:25,700 --> 00:55:26,250
Thanks.

740
00:55:26,250 --> 00:55:29,320
Dr Banner is only here to track the Cube.

741
00:55:29,320 --> 00:55:30,960
I was hoping you might join him.

742
00:55:30,960 --> 00:55:32,250
I would start with that stick of his.

743
00:55:32,250 --> 00:55:33,210
It may be magical,

744
00:55:33,210 --> 00:55:34,770
but it works an awful lot like a HYDRA weapon.

745
00:55:34,770 --> 00:55:37,830
I don't know about that, but it is powered by the Cube.

746
00:55:38,240 --> 00:55:40,180
And I would like to know how Loki used it

747
00:55:40,180 --> 00:55:43,780
to turn two of the sharpest men I know into his personal flying monkeys.

748
00:55:44,100 --> 00:55:45,830
Monkeys? I do not understand.

749
00:55:45,830 --> 00:55:46,670
I do.

750
00:55:50,210 --> 00:55:51,590
I understood that reference.

751
00:55:52,550 --> 00:55:53,620
Shall we play, Doctor?

752
00:55:54,240 --> 00:55:55,160
This way, sir.

753
00:56:09,800 --> 00:56:13,330
The gamma readings are definitely consistent with Selvig's reports of the Tesseract.

754
00:56:13,770 --> 00:56:15,690
But it's going to take weeks to process.

755
00:56:15,690 --> 00:56:18,520
If we bypass their mainframe and direct route to the Homer cluster,

756
00:56:18,520 --> 00:56:21,370
we can clock this at around 600 teraflops.

757
00:56:22,860 --> 00:56:24,720
All I packed was a toothbrush.

758
00:56:25,920 --> 00:56:27,650
You know, you should come by Stark Tower sometime.

759
00:56:27,650 --> 00:56:29,930
Top ten floors, all R&D.

760
00:56:29,930 --> 00:56:31,310
You'd love it. It's Candy Land.

761
00:56:31,730 --> 00:56:33,860
Thanks, but the last time I was in New York,

762
00:56:33,860 --> 00:56:36,890
I kind of broke Harlem.

763
00:56:37,370 --> 00:56:39,170
Well, I promise a stress-free environment.

764
00:56:39,170 --> 00:56:41,080
No tension, no surprises.

765
00:56:42,610 --> 00:56:43,200
Hey!

766
00:56:43,540 --> 00:56:44,150
Nothing?

767
00:56:44,150 --> 00:56:45,260
Are you nuts?

768
00:56:45,260 --> 00:56:46,040
Jury's out.

769
00:56:46,480 --> 00:56:47,840
You really have got a lid on it, haven't you?

770
00:56:47,840 --> 00:56:48,460
What's your secret?

771
00:56:48,460 --> 00:56:50,290
Mellow jazz, bongo drums, huge bag of weed?

772
00:56:50,290 --> 00:56:51,720
Is everything a joke to you?

773
00:56:52,070 --> 00:56:52,950
Funny things are.

774
00:56:52,950 --> 00:56:55,770
Threatening the safety of everyone on this ship isn't funny.

775
00:56:56,350 --> 00:56:57,170
No offence, Doc.

776
00:56:57,170 --> 00:57:01,330
It's all right, I wouldn't have come aboard if I couldn't handle pointy things.

777
00:57:02,190 --> 00:57:04,690
You're tip-toeing, big man. You need to strut.

778
00:57:04,690 --> 00:57:06,470
And you need to focus on the problem, Mr Stark.

779
00:57:06,470 --> 00:57:07,670
Do you think I'm not?

780
00:57:08,180 --> 00:57:10,980
Why did Fury call us in? Why now? Why not before?

781
00:57:10,980 --> 00:57:12,600
What isn't he telling us?

782
00:57:13,080 --> 00:57:14,950
I can't do the equation unless I have all the variables.

783
00:57:15,440 --> 00:57:16,720
You think Fury's hiding something?

784
00:57:16,720 --> 00:57:19,910
He's a spy. Captain, he's "the" spy.

785
00:57:19,910 --> 00:57:21,460
His secrets have secrets.

786
00:57:22,000 --> 00:57:23,450
It's bugging him, too. Isn't it?

787
00:57:25,860 --> 00:57:28,110
I just want to finish my work here, and...

788
00:57:28,110 --> 00:57:28,900
Doctor?

789
00:57:34,360 --> 00:57:36,590
"A warm light for all mankind."

790
00:57:37,020 --> 00:57:39,150
Loki's jab at Fury about the Cube.

791
00:57:39,150 --> 00:57:40,000
I heard it.

792
00:57:40,000 --> 00:57:41,800
I think that was meant for you.

793
00:57:43,670 --> 00:57:47,990
Even if Barton didn't tell Loki about the tower, it was still all over the news.

794
00:57:47,990 --> 00:57:50,300
The Stark Tower? That big, ugly

795
00:57:51,670 --> 00:57:52,660
building in New York?

796
00:57:52,660 --> 00:57:55,500
It's powered by an arc reactor, a self-sustaining energy source.

797
00:57:56,560 --> 00:57:58,530
That building will run itself for, what, a year?

798
00:57:59,190 --> 00:58:00,190
It's just the prototype.

799
00:58:01,130 --> 00:58:03,070
I'm kind of the only name in clean energy right now.

800
00:58:03,590 --> 00:58:04,340
That's what he's getting at.

801
00:58:04,340 --> 00:58:07,690
So, why didn't S.H.I.E.L.D. Bring him in on the Tesseract project?

802
00:58:07,690 --> 00:58:10,700
What are they doing in the energy business in the first place?

803
00:58:11,160 --> 00:58:12,720
I should probably look into that

804
00:58:12,720 --> 00:58:16,620
once my decryption programme finishes breaking into all of S.H.I.E.L.D.'s secure files.

805
00:58:16,620 --> 00:58:17,600
I'm sorry. Did you say...

806
00:58:17,600 --> 00:58:19,660
Jarvis has been running it since I hit the bridge.

807
00:58:19,660 --> 00:58:22,690
In a few hours, I'll know every dirty secret S.H.I.E.L.D. Has ever tried to hide.

808
00:58:22,690 --> 00:58:23,480
Blueberry?

809
00:58:23,480 --> 00:58:25,680
Yet you're confused about why they didn't want you around.

810
00:58:25,680 --> 00:58:28,790
An intelligence organisation that fears intelligence?

811
00:58:28,790 --> 00:58:30,460
Historically, not awesome.

812
00:58:30,460 --> 00:58:32,310
I think Loki's trying to wind us up.

813
00:58:32,930 --> 00:58:34,620
This is a man who means to start a war

814
00:58:34,620 --> 00:58:36,290
and if we don't stay focused, he'll succeed.

815
00:58:37,400 --> 00:58:39,890
We have orders. We should follow them.

816
00:58:40,350 --> 00:58:41,710
Following's not really my style.

817
00:58:43,680 --> 00:58:45,370
And you're all about style, aren't you?

818
00:58:46,150 --> 00:58:47,030
Of the people in this room,

819
00:58:47,030 --> 00:58:49,060
which one is, A, wearing a spangly outfit,

820
00:58:49,060 --> 00:58:50,470
and, B, not of use?

821
00:58:50,470 --> 00:58:54,820
Steve, tell me none of this smells a little funky to you.

822
00:58:57,770 --> 00:58:58,840
Just find the Cube.

823
00:59:11,430 --> 00:59:13,390
That's the guy my dad never shut up about?

824
00:59:14,020 --> 00:59:15,910
I'm wondering if they shouldn't have kept him on ice.

825
00:59:17,470 --> 00:59:19,330
The guy's not wrong about Loki.

826
00:59:19,330 --> 00:59:20,890
He does have the jump on us.

827
00:59:21,270 --> 00:59:23,880
What he's got is an Acme dynamite kit.

828
00:59:24,450 --> 00:59:25,670
It's going to blow up in his face.

829
00:59:26,090 --> 00:59:27,720
And I'm going to be there when it does.

830
00:59:28,610 --> 00:59:30,530
Yeah. I'll read all about it.

831
00:59:32,830 --> 00:59:34,370
Or you'll be suiting up with the rest of us.

832
00:59:35,790 --> 00:59:39,170
You see, I don't get a suit of armour.

833
00:59:39,540 --> 00:59:43,030
I'm exposed. Like a nerve.

834
00:59:43,030 --> 00:59:44,280
It's a nightmare.

835
00:59:44,930 --> 00:59:49,660
You know, I've got a cluster of shrapnel trying every second to crawl its way into my heart.

836
00:59:50,050 --> 00:59:51,530
This stops it.

837
00:59:52,160 --> 00:59:54,540
This little circle of light, it's part of me now,

838
00:59:55,590 --> 00:59:56,810
not just armour.

839
00:59:57,930 --> 01:00:00,210
It's a terrible privilege.

840
01:00:00,710 --> 01:00:02,330
But you can control it.

841
01:00:02,330 --> 01:00:03,450
Because I learned how.

842
01:00:03,450 --> 01:00:04,190
It's different.

843
01:00:04,500 --> 01:00:07,750
Hey, I read all about your accident.

844
01:00:08,080 --> 01:00:11,220
That much gamma exposure should have killed you.

845
01:00:11,640 --> 01:00:13,670
So you're saying that the Hulk...

846
01:00:15,420 --> 01:00:17,650
The other guy saved my life?

847
01:00:18,310 --> 01:00:19,230
That's nice.

848
01:00:20,290 --> 01:00:23,690
It's a nice sentiment. Saved it for what?

849
01:00:25,450 --> 01:00:26,740
I guess we'll find out.

850
01:00:29,010 --> 01:00:30,750
You may not enjoy that.

851
01:00:30,750 --> 01:00:32,270
And you just might.

852
01:01:32,130 --> 01:01:35,140
As soon as Loki took the doctor, we moved Jane Foster.

853
01:01:35,610 --> 01:01:37,800
They've got an excellent observatory in Troms?

854
01:01:37,800 --> 01:01:40,940
She was asked to consult there very suddenly yesterday.

855
01:01:41,340 --> 01:01:45,140
Handsome fee, private plane, very remote.

856
01:01:46,100 --> 01:01:47,070
She'll be safe.

857
01:01:47,070 --> 01:01:48,200
Thank you.

858
01:01:50,550 --> 01:01:52,470
It's no accident, Loki taking Erik Selvig.

859
01:01:53,610 --> 01:01:55,980
I dread what he plans for him once he's done.

860
01:01:56,430 --> 01:01:57,720
Erik is a good man.

861
01:01:57,720 --> 01:01:58,990
He talks about you a lot.

862
01:02:00,450 --> 01:02:01,830
You changed his life.

863
01:02:04,140 --> 01:02:05,750
You changed everything around here.

864
01:02:06,270 --> 01:02:08,030
They were better as they were.

865
01:02:08,890 --> 01:02:11,250
We pretend on Asgard that we're more advanced

866
01:02:11,250 --> 01:02:14,680
but we come here, battling like bilge snipe.

867
01:02:14,680 --> 01:02:15,400
Like what?

868
01:02:15,670 --> 01:02:16,920
Bilge snipe.

869
01:02:16,920 --> 01:02:20,270
You know, huge, scaly, big antlers.

870
01:02:20,710 --> 01:02:21,660
You don't have those?

871
01:02:21,660 --> 01:02:22,760
I don't think so.

872
01:02:22,760 --> 01:02:24,270
Well, they are repulsive.

873
01:02:25,860 --> 01:02:27,640
And they trample everything in their path.

874
01:02:35,730 --> 01:02:39,360
When I first came to Earth, Loki's rage followed me here,

875
01:02:39,360 --> 01:02:41,100
and your people paid the price.

876
01:02:41,680 --> 01:02:43,150
And now, again.

877
01:02:46,030 --> 01:02:48,410
In my youth, I courted war.

878
01:02:50,320 --> 01:02:51,910
War hasn't started yet.

879
01:02:53,630 --> 01:02:56,580
You think you could make Loki tell us where the Tesseract is?

880
01:02:56,580 --> 01:03:00,170
I do not know. Loki's mind is far afield.

881
01:03:00,170 --> 01:03:04,310
It's not just power he craves, it's vengeance, upon me.

882
01:03:04,930 --> 01:03:07,220
There's no pain would prise his need from him.

883
01:03:08,140 --> 01:03:09,680
A lot of guys think that

884
01:03:10,520 --> 01:03:12,040
until the pain starts.

885
01:03:14,270 --> 01:03:15,820
What are you asking me to do?

886
01:03:15,820 --> 01:03:19,590
I'm asking, what are you prepared to do?

887
01:03:19,590 --> 01:03:20,740
Loki is a prisoner.

888
01:03:20,760 --> 01:03:24,730
Then why do I feel like he's the only person on this boat that wants to be here?

889
01:03:37,410 --> 01:03:40,120
There's not many people who can sneak up on me.

890
01:03:40,680 --> 01:03:42,170
But you figured I'd come.

891
01:03:43,010 --> 01:03:44,090
After.

892
01:03:45,430 --> 01:03:48,880
After whatever tortures Fury can concoct,

893
01:03:48,880 --> 01:03:52,410
you would appear as a friend, as a balm.

894
01:03:53,670 --> 01:03:55,150
And I would cooperate.

895
01:03:55,370 --> 01:03:57,390
I want to know what you've done to Agent Barton.

896
01:03:57,870 --> 01:04:00,160
I would say I've expanded his mind.

897
01:04:02,140 --> 01:04:04,010
And once you've won,

898
01:04:04,930 --> 01:04:06,540
once you're king of the mountain,

899
01:04:08,320 --> 01:04:10,780
what happens to his mind?

900
01:04:12,210 --> 01:04:14,030
Is this love, Agent Romanoff?

901
01:04:14,030 --> 01:04:16,720
Love is for children. I owe him a debt.

902
01:04:20,720 --> 01:04:21,390
Tell me.

903
01:04:26,880 --> 01:04:30,420
Before I worked for S.H.I.E.L.D... I...

904
01:04:32,590 --> 01:04:36,320
Well, I made a name for myself.

905
01:04:36,720 --> 01:04:39,230
I have a very specific skill set.

906
01:04:39,740 --> 01:04:43,520
I didn't care who I used it for, or on.

907
01:04:44,520 --> 01:04:47,610
I got on S.H.I.E.L.D.'s radar in a bad way.

908
01:04:49,060 --> 01:04:51,490
Agent Barton was sent to kill me.

909
01:04:53,130 --> 01:04:54,630
He made a different call.

910
01:04:56,640 --> 01:04:59,440
And what will you do if I vow to spare him?

911
01:04:59,810 --> 01:05:00,870
Not let you out.

912
01:05:00,870 --> 01:05:03,470
No, but I like this.

913
01:05:04,240 --> 01:05:07,790
Your world in the balance, and you bargain for one man.

914
01:05:07,790 --> 01:05:09,740
Regimes fall every day.

915
01:05:10,090 --> 01:05:12,390
I tend not to weep over that. I'm Russian.

916
01:05:12,590 --> 01:05:13,660
Or I was.

917
01:05:14,980 --> 01:05:16,430
And what are you now?

918
01:05:17,190 --> 01:05:19,130
It's really not that complicated.

919
01:05:20,190 --> 01:05:24,290
I got red in my ledger, I'd like to wipe it out.

920
01:05:25,230 --> 01:05:26,580
Can you?

921
01:05:28,150 --> 01:05:31,750
Can you wipe out that much red?

922
01:05:33,180 --> 01:05:34,920
Dreykov's daughter,

923
01:05:36,280 --> 01:05:37,370
Sao Paulo,

924
01:05:39,220 --> 01:05:41,010
the hospital fire?

925
01:05:42,570 --> 01:05:44,510
Barton told me everything.

926
01:05:44,960 --> 01:05:48,280
Your ledger is dripping. It's gushing red

927
01:05:48,280 --> 01:05:52,180
and you think saving a man no more virtuous than yourself will change anything?

928
01:05:52,180 --> 01:05:55,120
This is the basest sentimentality.

929
01:05:55,120 --> 01:05:57,460
This is a child at prayer.

930
01:05:57,460 --> 01:05:58,890
Pathetic!

931
01:05:59,660 --> 01:06:02,270
You lie and kill

932
01:06:02,270 --> 01:06:05,680
in the service of liars and killers.

933
01:06:08,480 --> 01:06:11,640
You pretend to be separate, to have your own code,

934
01:06:12,080 --> 01:06:13,800
something that makes up for the horrors.

935
01:06:15,680 --> 01:06:17,550
But they are part of you.

936
01:06:18,240 --> 01:06:21,740
And they will never go away.

937
01:06:22,950 --> 01:06:26,190
I won't touch Barton, not until I make him kill you.

938
01:06:26,190 --> 01:06:28,470
Slowly, intimately,

939
01:06:28,470 --> 01:06:30,970
in every way he knows you fear.

940
01:06:30,970 --> 01:06:34,260
And then he'll wake just long enough to see his good work

941
01:06:34,260 --> 01:06:37,370
and when he screams, I'll split his skull.

942
01:06:37,850 --> 01:06:40,830
This is my bargain, you mewling quim.

943
01:06:42,600 --> 01:06:44,200
You're a monster.

944
01:06:46,400 --> 01:06:47,820
Oh, no.

945
01:06:48,840 --> 01:06:50,690
You brought the monster.

946
01:06:53,410 --> 01:06:54,940
So, Banner.

947
01:06:56,000 --> 01:06:57,370
That's your play.

948
01:06:57,800 --> 01:06:58,460
What?

949
01:06:59,160 --> 01:07:00,850
Loki means to unleash the Hulk.

950
01:07:00,850 --> 01:07:02,370
Keep Banner in the lab. I'm on my way.

951
01:07:02,370 --> 01:07:03,480
Send Thor as well.

952
01:07:05,390 --> 01:07:06,360
Thank you

953
01:07:06,880 --> 01:07:08,710
for your cooperation.

954
01:07:16,510 --> 01:07:18,080
What are you doing, Mr Stark?

955
01:07:18,570 --> 01:07:20,760
Kind of been wondering the same thing about you.

956
01:07:20,760 --> 01:07:22,700
You're supposed to be locating the Tesseract.

957
01:07:22,700 --> 01:07:25,790
We are. The model's locked and we're sweeping for the signature now.

958
01:07:25,790 --> 01:07:29,020
When we get a hit, we'll have the location within half a mile.

959
01:07:29,020 --> 01:07:32,620
Yeah, then you get your Cube back. No muss, no fuss.

960
01:07:33,470 --> 01:07:34,580
What is "Phase 2"?

961
01:07:36,860 --> 01:07:39,630
Phase 2 is S.H.I.E.L.D. Uses the Cube to make weapons.

962
01:07:39,630 --> 01:07:41,740
Sorry, computer was moving a little slow for me.

963
01:07:41,740 --> 01:07:44,610
Rogers, we gathered everything related to the Tesseract.

964
01:07:44,610 --> 01:07:45,720
This does not mean that we're making...

965
01:07:45,720 --> 01:07:46,660
I'm sorry, Nick.

966
01:07:47,010 --> 01:07:48,300
What were you lying?

967
01:07:49,630 --> 01:07:50,920
I was wrong, Director.

968
01:07:50,920 --> 01:07:52,270
The world hasn't changed a bit.

969
01:07:52,270 --> 01:07:53,330
Did you know about this?

970
01:07:53,330 --> 01:07:55,960
You want to think about removing yourself from this environment, Doctor?

971
01:07:56,300 --> 01:07:58,480
I was in Calcutta. I was pretty well removed.

972
01:07:58,480 --> 01:07:59,840
Loki is manipulating you.

973
01:07:59,840 --> 01:08:01,240
And you've been doing what, exactly?

974
01:08:01,240 --> 01:08:03,300
You didn't come here because I bat my eyelashes at you.

975
01:08:03,300 --> 01:08:05,870
Yes, and I'm not leaving because suddenly you get a little twitchy.

976
01:08:05,870 --> 01:08:11,420
I'd like to know why S.H.I.E.L.D. is using the Tesseract to build weapons of mass destruction.

977
01:08:12,090 --> 01:08:13,220
Because of him.

978
01:08:14,730 --> 01:08:15,460
Me?

979
01:08:16,450 --> 01:08:18,940
Last year, Earth had a visitor from another planet

980
01:08:18,940 --> 01:08:22,210
who had a grudge match that levelled a small town.

981
01:08:22,210 --> 01:08:24,500
We learned that not only are we not alone

982
01:08:24,500 --> 01:08:28,350
but we are hopelessly, hilariously, outgunned.

983
01:08:28,350 --> 01:08:30,520
My people want nothing but peace with your planet.

984
01:08:30,520 --> 01:08:32,760
But you're not the only people out there, are you?

985
01:08:32,760 --> 01:08:34,940
And you're not the only threat.

986
01:08:34,940 --> 01:08:38,190
The world's filling up with people who can't be matched,

987
01:08:38,720 --> 01:08:39,880
that can't be controlled.

988
01:08:39,880 --> 01:08:41,240
Like you controlled the Cube?

989
01:08:41,240 --> 01:08:45,370
Your work with the Tesseract is what drew Loki to it, and his allies.

990
01:08:45,370 --> 01:08:47,060
It is a signal to all the realms

991
01:08:47,060 --> 01:08:49,690
that the Earth is ready for a higher form of war.

992
01:08:49,690 --> 01:08:50,900
A higher form?

993
01:08:50,900 --> 01:08:52,140
You forced our hand.

994
01:08:52,140 --> 01:08:53,010
We had to come up with something.

995
01:08:53,010 --> 01:08:54,230
A nuclear deterrent.

996
01:08:54,230 --> 01:08:56,320
Because that always calms everything right down.

997
01:08:56,320 --> 01:08:58,900
Remind me again how you made your fortune, Stark.

998
01:08:58,900 --> 01:09:01,090
I'm sure if he still made weapons, Stark would be neck-deep...

999
01:09:01,090 --> 01:09:02,890
Hold on. How is this now about me?

1000
01:09:02,890 --> 01:09:04,360
I'm sorry, isn't everything?

1001
01:09:04,360 --> 01:09:06,550
I thought humans were more evolved than this.

1002
01:09:06,550 --> 01:09:09,390
Excuse me, did we come to your planet and blow stuff up?

1003
01:09:09,390 --> 01:09:11,520
You treat your champions with such mistrust.

1004
01:09:11,520 --> 01:09:13,050
Are you boys really that naive?

1005
01:09:13,050 --> 01:09:15,010
S.H.I.E.L.D. Monitors potential threats.

1006
01:09:15,010 --> 01:09:16,640
Captain America's on threat watch?

1007
01:09:16,640 --> 01:09:17,430
We all are.

1008
01:09:17,430 --> 01:09:18,710
Wait, you're on that list?

1009
01:09:18,710 --> 01:09:20,910
Are you above or below angry bees?

1010
01:09:20,910 --> 01:09:22,750
Stark, so help me God, if you make one more wisecrack...

1011
01:09:22,750 --> 01:09:24,360
Threat! Verbal threat. I feel threatened.

1012
01:09:24,360 --> 01:09:25,240
Show some respect.

1013
01:09:25,240 --> 01:09:26,980
Respect what?

1014
01:09:33,970 --> 01:09:36,950
Transport Six-Six-Bravo, please relay confirm codes.

1015
01:09:36,950 --> 01:09:39,260
I've got you on the computer, but not on the day log.

1016
01:09:39,260 --> 01:09:40,790
What is your haul? Over.

1017
01:09:41,520 --> 01:09:43,200
Arms and ammunition. Over.

1018
01:09:52,440 --> 01:09:54,940
You speak of control, yet you court chaos.

1019
01:09:54,940 --> 01:09:56,170
That's his M.O., isn't it?

1020
01:09:56,630 --> 01:09:57,940
I mean, what are we, a team?

1021
01:09:57,940 --> 01:10:00,850
No, we're a chemical mixture that makes chaos.

1022
01:10:00,850 --> 01:10:03,100
We're a time bomb.

1023
01:10:03,100 --> 01:10:05,020
You need to step away.

1024
01:10:05,020 --> 01:10:07,000
Why shouldn't the guy let off a little steam?

1025
01:10:07,000 --> 01:10:09,050
You know damn well why. Back off!

1026
01:10:09,490 --> 01:10:11,040
I'm starting to want you to make me.

1027
01:10:11,650 --> 01:10:14,180
Yeah. Big man in a suit of armour.

1028
01:10:15,610 --> 01:10:16,980
Take that off, what are you?

1029
01:10:17,210 --> 01:10:19,510
Genius, billionaire, playboy, philanthropist.

1030
01:10:20,210 --> 01:10:23,040
I know guys with none of that worth ten of you.

1031
01:10:23,550 --> 01:10:24,760
I've seen the footage.

1032
01:10:24,760 --> 01:10:27,150
The only thing you really fight for is yourself.

1033
01:10:28,190 --> 01:10:30,070
You're not the guy to make the sacrifice play,

1034
01:10:30,390 --> 01:10:32,970
to lay down on a wire and let the other guy crawl over you.

1035
01:10:32,970 --> 01:10:34,490
I think I would just cut the wire.

1036
01:10:37,790 --> 01:10:38,780
Always a way out.

1037
01:10:40,110 --> 01:10:43,260
You may not be a threat but you better stop pretending to be a hero.

1038
01:10:43,710 --> 01:10:45,220
A hero? Like you?

1039
01:10:46,140 --> 01:10:48,070
You're a laboratory experiment, Rogers.

1040
01:10:48,070 --> 01:10:51,340
Everything special about you came out of a bottle.

1041
01:11:17,260 --> 01:11:19,230
Put on the suit. Let's go a few rounds.

1042
01:11:21,290 --> 01:11:24,770
You people are so petty and tiny.

1043
01:11:24,770 --> 01:11:25,880
Yeah, this is a team.

1044
01:11:25,880 --> 01:11:28,300
Agent Romanoff, would you escort Dr Banner back to his...

1045
01:11:28,300 --> 01:11:30,360
Where? You rented my room.

1046
01:11:30,360 --> 01:11:31,930
The cell was just in case...

1047
01:11:31,930 --> 01:11:33,330
In case you needed to kill me.

1048
01:11:33,330 --> 01:11:35,810
But you can't. I know, I tried.

1049
01:11:39,050 --> 01:11:42,150
I got low. I didn't see an end.

1050
01:11:42,150 --> 01:11:46,040
So, I put a bullet in my mouth, and the other guy spit it out.

1051
01:11:47,290 --> 01:11:48,460
So I moved on.

1052
01:11:48,460 --> 01:11:51,610
I focused on helping other people. I was good.

1053
01:11:51,610 --> 01:11:54,080
Until you dragged me back into this freak show

1054
01:11:54,080 --> 01:11:55,690
and put everyone here at risk.

1055
01:11:55,690 --> 01:11:57,440
You want to know my secret, Agent Romanoff?

1056
01:11:57,440 --> 01:11:59,190
You want to know how I stay calm?

1057
01:12:02,410 --> 01:12:03,170
Dr Banner,

1058
01:12:05,220 --> 01:12:06,510
put down the sceptre.

1059
01:12:15,240 --> 01:12:15,850
Got it.

1060
01:12:17,630 --> 01:12:20,410
Sorry, kids, you don't get to see my party trick after all.

1061
01:12:20,410 --> 01:12:21,360
You located the Tesseract?

1062
01:12:21,360 --> 01:12:22,160
I could get there fastest.

1063
01:12:22,160 --> 01:12:24,670
The Tesseract belongs on Asgard. No human is a match for it.

1064
01:12:24,670 --> 01:12:25,500
You're not going alone

1065
01:12:25,500 --> 01:12:26,180
You're gonna stop me?

1066
01:12:26,180 --> 01:12:27,300
Put on the suit, let's find out.

1067
01:12:27,300 --> 01:12:28,790
I'm not afraid to hit an old man.

1068
01:12:28,790 --> 01:12:29,780
Put on the suit.

1069
01:12:32,620 --> 01:12:33,460
Oh, my God.

1070
01:12:49,680 --> 01:12:50,570
Put on the suit.

1071
01:12:50,570 --> 01:12:51,280
Yeah.

1072
01:12:54,810 --> 01:12:56,230
All hands to stations.

1073
01:13:00,720 --> 01:13:01,350
Hill!

1074
01:13:01,350 --> 01:13:04,550
External detonation. Number three engine is down.

1075
01:13:04,550 --> 01:13:05,270
We've been hit.

1076
01:13:05,270 --> 01:13:06,140
Can they get it running?

1077
01:13:06,140 --> 01:13:06,960
Fire in engine three!

1078
01:13:06,960 --> 01:13:07,560
Talk to me.

1079
01:13:07,560 --> 01:13:09,420
Turbine looks mostly intact

1080
01:13:09,420 --> 01:13:12,310
but it's impossible to get out there to make repairs while we're in the air.

1081
01:13:12,970 --> 01:13:14,820
If we lose one more engine, we won't be.

1082
01:13:15,580 --> 01:13:17,780
Somebody's got to get outside and patch that engine.

1083
01:13:17,780 --> 01:13:18,770
Stark, you copy that?

1084
01:13:18,770 --> 01:13:19,460
I'm on it.

1085
01:13:19,460 --> 01:13:22,980
Coulson, initiate defensive lockdown in the detention section

1086
01:13:22,980 --> 01:13:24,030
then get to the armoury.

1087
01:13:24,510 --> 01:13:25,460
Romanoff?

1088
01:13:28,780 --> 01:13:29,690
We're okay.

1089
01:13:32,910 --> 01:13:33,980
We're okay, right?

1090
01:13:46,710 --> 01:13:47,650
Keep that engine down!

1091
01:13:47,650 --> 01:13:48,210
Yes, sir.

1092
01:13:48,210 --> 01:13:49,840
Detention, wait for cameras to go dark.

1093
01:13:49,840 --> 01:13:50,410
Got it.

1094
01:13:50,410 --> 01:13:51,030
Stay close.

1095
01:13:53,640 --> 01:13:55,030
Let's go, Level 4.

1096
01:13:55,870 --> 01:13:57,630
Engine three. I'll meet you there.

1097
01:14:07,000 --> 01:14:07,710
Doctor?

1098
01:14:10,330 --> 01:14:11,110
Bruce?

1099
01:14:11,830 --> 01:14:14,680
You got to fight it. This is just what Loki wants.

1100
01:14:16,700 --> 01:14:18,120
We're going to be okay. Listen to me.

1101
01:14:18,500 --> 01:14:19,330
Are you hurt?

1102
01:14:22,420 --> 01:14:24,320
We're going to be okay. All right?

1103
01:14:25,090 --> 01:14:27,580
I swear on my life, I will get you out of this.

1104
01:14:27,580 --> 01:14:29,010
You will walk away and never ever...

1105
01:14:29,010 --> 01:14:30,500
Your life?

1106
01:14:47,870 --> 01:14:48,870
Bruce.

1107
01:15:25,390 --> 01:15:27,930
Bring the carrier about to a 1-8-0, heading south!

1108
01:15:28,740 --> 01:15:29,800
Take us to the water!

1109
01:15:29,800 --> 01:15:30,670
We're flying blind.

1110
01:15:30,670 --> 01:15:32,720
Navigation's recalibrating after the engine failure.

1111
01:15:32,720 --> 01:15:34,200
Is the sun coming up?

1112
01:15:35,380 --> 01:15:35,900
Yes, sir.

1113
01:15:35,900 --> 01:15:37,710
Then put it on the left.

1114
01:15:37,710 --> 01:15:39,460
Get us over water.

1115
01:15:39,460 --> 01:15:41,460
One more turbine goes down, and we drop.

1116
01:15:43,920 --> 01:15:44,460
Thanks.

1117
01:15:48,540 --> 01:15:49,410
Stark!

1118
01:15:52,330 --> 01:15:53,610
Stark, I'm here!

1119
01:15:54,220 --> 01:15:54,740
Good.

1120
01:15:56,920 --> 01:15:57,910
Let's see what we've got.

1121
01:15:59,030 --> 01:16:01,900
I got to get this superconducting coolant system back online

1122
01:16:01,900 --> 01:16:05,100
before I can access the rotors, work on dislodging the debris.

1123
01:16:07,890 --> 01:16:09,370
I need you to get to that engine control panel

1124
01:16:09,370 --> 01:16:11,560
and tell me which relays are in overload position.

1125
01:16:25,580 --> 01:16:26,620
What does it look like in there?

1126
01:16:27,720 --> 01:16:30,350
It seems to run on some form of electricity.

1127
01:16:30,350 --> 01:16:31,570
Well, you're not wrong.

1128
01:17:36,060 --> 01:17:38,610
We are not your enemies, Banner.

1129
01:17:39,060 --> 01:17:40,450
Try to think!

1130
01:17:50,190 --> 01:17:51,630
Okay, the relays are intact.

1131
01:17:52,350 --> 01:17:53,290
What's our next move?

1132
01:17:53,840 --> 01:17:54,860
Even if I clear the rotors,

1133
01:17:54,860 --> 01:17:56,710
this thing won't re-engage without a jump.

1134
01:17:57,200 --> 01:17:58,590
I'm going to have to get in there and push.

1135
01:17:58,590 --> 01:18:00,360
If that thing gets up to speed, you'll get shredded.

1136
01:18:00,360 --> 01:18:02,520
That stator control unit can reverse the polarity

1137
01:18:02,520 --> 01:18:04,290
long enough to disengage maglev and that could...

1138
01:18:04,290 --> 01:18:05,370
Speak English!

1139
01:18:06,910 --> 01:18:08,250
You see that red lever?

1140
01:18:09,370 --> 01:18:11,560
It will slow the rotors down long enough for me to get out.

1141
01:18:11,560 --> 01:18:13,470
Stand by it. Wait for my word.

1142
01:19:05,940 --> 01:19:07,640
We need full evac on the lower hangar bay.

1143
01:19:11,140 --> 01:19:11,560
Grenade!

1144
01:19:27,170 --> 01:19:28,370
We've got a perimeter breach!

1145
01:19:28,790 --> 01:19:30,530
Hostiles are in S.H.I.E.L.D. Gear.

1146
01:19:30,530 --> 01:19:31,790
Call-outs at every junction.

1147
01:19:40,280 --> 01:19:42,610
We have the Hulk and Thor on Research Level 4.

1148
01:19:42,610 --> 01:19:44,050
Levels 2 and 3 are dark.

1149
01:19:44,050 --> 01:19:45,760
Sir, the Hulk will tear this place apart!

1150
01:19:47,680 --> 01:19:48,700
Get his attention.

1151
01:19:48,700 --> 01:19:52,410
Escort 6-0, proceed to Wishbone and engage hostile.

1152
01:19:52,930 --> 01:19:53,960
Don't get too close.

1153
01:19:54,510 --> 01:19:55,210
Copy.

1154
01:20:07,500 --> 01:20:08,500
Target acquired.

1155
01:20:13,530 --> 01:20:14,610
Target engaged.

1156
01:20:26,000 --> 01:20:27,570
Target angry, target angry!

1157
01:21:36,080 --> 01:21:38,240
They're not getting through here, so what the hell...

1158
01:21:56,440 --> 01:21:58,010
Engine one is now in shut-down.

1159
01:22:07,220 --> 01:22:09,190
We are in an uncontrolled descent.

1160
01:22:09,590 --> 01:22:11,410
Sir, we've lost all power in engine one.

1161
01:22:11,860 --> 01:22:13,790
It's Barton. He took out our systems.

1162
01:22:13,790 --> 01:22:15,370
He's headed for the detention level.

1163
01:22:16,520 --> 01:22:17,560
Does anybody copy?

1164
01:22:19,610 --> 01:22:20,830
This is Agent Romanoff.

1165
01:22:21,980 --> 01:22:23,140
I copy.

1166
01:22:27,890 --> 01:22:29,320
Stark, we're losing altitude.

1167
01:22:29,320 --> 01:22:30,440
Yeah, I noticed.

1168
01:22:59,420 --> 01:23:00,360
No!

1169
01:23:08,180 --> 01:23:10,360
Are you ever not going to fall for that?

1170
01:23:53,810 --> 01:23:55,570
The humans think us immortal.

1171
01:23:57,250 --> 01:23:58,240
Should we test that?

1172
01:24:01,520 --> 01:24:02,320
Move away, please.

1173
01:24:07,180 --> 01:24:08,060
You like this?

1174
01:24:09,720 --> 01:24:12,240
We started working on the prototype after you sent the Destroyer.

1175
01:24:14,180 --> 01:24:15,500
Even I don't know what it does.

1176
01:24:17,180 --> 01:24:18,120
Do you want to find out?

1177
01:24:20,390 --> 01:24:21,640
No!

1178
01:25:31,620 --> 01:25:32,380
Natasha?

1179
01:26:04,540 --> 01:26:05,640
You're going to lose.

1180
01:26:08,200 --> 01:26:09,200
Am I?

1181
01:26:10,870 --> 01:26:12,160
It's in your nature.

1182
01:26:15,420 --> 01:26:17,070
Your heroes are scattered.

1183
01:26:17,930 --> 01:26:20,670
Your floating fortress falls from the sky.

1184
01:26:21,720 --> 01:26:23,310
Where is my disadvantage?

1185
01:26:24,120 --> 01:26:25,720
You lack conviction.

1186
01:26:27,010 --> 01:26:27,690
I don't think I'm...

1187
01:26:34,790 --> 01:26:36,340
So, that's what it does.

1188
01:26:38,540 --> 01:26:41,060
All hands to crash stations immediately.

1189
01:27:09,190 --> 01:27:10,090
Cap, hit the lever.

1190
01:27:10,790 --> 01:27:11,820
I need a minute here!

1191
01:27:13,330 --> 01:27:14,000
Lever

1192
01:27:14,610 --> 01:27:15,420
now!

1193
01:27:27,590 --> 01:27:28,380
Help!

1194
01:28:04,410 --> 01:28:05,190
Sorry, boss.

1195
01:28:05,950 --> 01:28:07,230
The god rabbited.

1196
01:28:07,940 --> 01:28:08,900
Just stay awake.

1197
01:28:09,360 --> 01:28:10,800
Eyes on me.

1198
01:28:11,400 --> 01:28:12,780
No, I'm clocking out here.

1199
01:28:12,780 --> 01:28:13,970
Not an option.

1200
01:28:15,270 --> 01:28:16,640
It's okay, boss.

1201
01:28:19,120 --> 01:28:20,660
This was never gonna work

1202
01:28:21,460 --> 01:28:23,020
if they didn't have something

1203
01:28:24,030 --> 01:28:25,030
to...

1204
01:28:54,590 --> 01:28:56,050
Agent Coulson is down.

1205
01:28:57,870 --> 01:28:59,620
A medical team is on its way to your location.

1206
01:28:59,620 --> 01:29:00,330
They're here.

1207
01:29:04,400 --> 01:29:05,420
They called it.

1208
01:29:22,400 --> 01:29:24,520
These were in Phil Coulson's jacket.

1209
01:29:27,420 --> 01:29:29,300
I guess he never did get you to sign them.

1210
01:29:33,010 --> 01:29:34,020
We're dead in the air up here.

1211
01:29:34,880 --> 01:29:37,570
Our communications, the location of the Cube,

1212
01:29:38,110 --> 01:29:40,430
Banner, Thor...

1213
01:29:41,810 --> 01:29:43,320
I got nothing for you

1214
01:29:43,850 --> 01:29:45,960
I lost my one good eye.

1215
01:29:49,770 --> 01:29:51,280
Maybe I had that coming.

1216
01:29:56,990 --> 01:29:57,940
Yes,

1217
01:29:59,430 --> 01:30:02,860
we were going to build an arsenal with the Tesseract.

1218
01:30:04,200 --> 01:30:06,380
I never put all my chips on that number, though

1219
01:30:06,380 --> 01:30:08,650
because I was playing something even riskier.

1220
01:30:13,210 --> 01:30:17,380
There was an idea, Stark knows this,

1221
01:30:19,270 --> 01:30:21,940
called the Avengers Initiative.

1222
01:30:23,800 --> 01:30:27,950
The idea was to bring together a group of remarkable people

1223
01:30:29,390 --> 01:30:31,500
to see if they could become something more.

1224
01:30:33,620 --> 01:30:36,620
To see if they could work together when we needed them to,

1225
01:30:37,550 --> 01:30:40,110
to fight the battles that we never could.

1226
01:30:43,980 --> 01:30:48,290
Phil Coulson died still believing in that idea.

1227
01:30:51,150 --> 01:30:52,430
In heroes.

1228
01:31:00,990 --> 01:31:01,910
Well,

1229
01:31:03,460 --> 01:31:05,860
it's an old-fashioned notion.

1230
01:31:26,470 --> 01:31:28,310
You fell out of the sky.

1231
01:31:42,850 --> 01:31:44,190
Did I hurt anybody?

1232
01:31:44,920 --> 01:31:46,680
There's nobody around here to get hurt.

1233
01:31:47,680 --> 01:31:50,090
You did scare the hell out of some pigeons, though.

1234
01:31:51,940 --> 01:31:52,890
Lucky.

1235
01:31:52,890 --> 01:31:54,770
Or just good aim.

1236
01:31:54,770 --> 01:31:56,670
You were awake when you fell.

1237
01:31:58,390 --> 01:31:59,190
You saw?

1238
01:31:59,190 --> 01:32:00,360
The whole thing.

1239
01:32:00,360 --> 01:32:01,700
Right through the ceiling.

1240
01:32:02,300 --> 01:32:05,620
Big and green and buck-ass nude.

1241
01:32:06,310 --> 01:32:07,010
Here.

1242
01:32:08,930 --> 01:32:13,000
Didn't think those would fit you until you shrunk down to a regular-size feller.

1243
01:32:15,980 --> 01:32:16,780
Thank you.

1244
01:32:18,540 --> 01:32:19,650
Are you an alien?

1245
01:32:20,050 --> 01:32:20,810
What?

1246
01:32:21,690 --> 01:32:23,190
From outer space, an alien.

1247
01:32:23,620 --> 01:32:24,240
No.

1248
01:32:24,900 --> 01:32:28,110
Well, then, son, you've got a condition.

1249
01:32:38,920 --> 01:32:41,470
Clint. You're going to be all right.

1250
01:32:44,640 --> 01:32:45,680
You know that?

1251
01:32:47,600 --> 01:32:48,770
Is that what you know?

1252
01:32:53,460 --> 01:32:54,620
I've got no window.

1253
01:32:55,780 --> 01:32:56,900
I have to flush him out.

1254
01:32:57,930 --> 01:32:59,780
You got to level out. It's going to take time.

1255
01:32:59,780 --> 01:33:01,000
You don't understand.

1256
01:33:03,390 --> 01:33:06,070
Have you ever had someone take your brain and play?

1257
01:33:07,350 --> 01:33:10,530
Pull you out and stuff something else in?

1258
01:33:14,700 --> 01:33:16,710
Do you know what it's like to be unmade?

1259
01:33:18,540 --> 01:33:19,830
You know that I do.

1260
01:33:28,560 --> 01:33:29,830
Why am I back?

1261
01:33:30,710 --> 01:33:32,000
How did you get him out?

1262
01:33:32,300 --> 01:33:34,010
Cognitive recalibration.

1263
01:33:35,040 --> 01:33:36,520
I hit you really hard on the head.

1264
01:33:38,320 --> 01:33:39,110
Thanks.

1265
01:33:43,450 --> 01:33:44,120
Natasha...

1266
01:33:45,950 --> 01:33:46,870
How many agents did I...

1267
01:33:46,870 --> 01:33:48,270
Don't.

1268
01:33:48,630 --> 01:33:50,860
Don't do that to yourself, Clint.

1269
01:33:51,450 --> 01:33:52,940
This is Loki.

1270
01:33:53,250 --> 01:33:55,940
This is monsters and magic,

1271
01:33:55,940 --> 01:33:57,980
and nothing we were ever trained for.

1272
01:33:57,980 --> 01:33:59,650
Loki, did he get away?

1273
01:33:59,650 --> 01:34:00,390
Yeah.

1274
01:34:00,720 --> 01:34:02,280
I don't suppose you know where.

1275
01:34:03,030 --> 01:34:04,060
I didn't need to know.

1276
01:34:05,040 --> 01:34:05,960
I didn't ask.

1277
01:34:10,140 --> 01:34:12,170
He's going to make his play soon, though.

1278
01:34:13,110 --> 01:34:14,130
Today.

1279
01:34:14,130 --> 01:34:15,230
We got to stop him.

1280
01:34:15,920 --> 01:34:17,270
Yeah? Who's "we"?

1281
01:34:17,270 --> 01:34:19,200
I don't know. Whoever's left.

1282
01:34:20,490 --> 01:34:21,650
Well,

1283
01:34:23,570 --> 01:34:26,330
if I put an arrow through Loki's eye socket,

1284
01:34:26,330 --> 01:34:27,890
I would sleep better, I suppose.

1285
01:34:31,350 --> 01:34:32,690
Now you sound like you.

1286
01:34:33,710 --> 01:34:35,060
But you don't.

1287
01:34:37,110 --> 01:34:39,660
You're a spy, not a soldier.

1288
01:34:40,050 --> 01:34:44,380
Now you want to wade into a war. Why?

1289
01:34:46,490 --> 01:34:47,880
What did Loki do to you?

1290
01:34:49,320 --> 01:34:51,550
He didn't. I just...

1291
01:34:55,520 --> 01:34:56,400
Natasha.

1292
01:34:59,070 --> 01:35:00,780
I've been compromised.

1293
01:35:04,120 --> 01:35:06,020
I got red in my ledger.

1294
01:35:08,270 --> 01:35:09,880
I would like to wipe it out.

1295
01:35:26,570 --> 01:35:27,670
Was he married?

1296
01:35:28,100 --> 01:35:28,840
No.

1297
01:35:29,730 --> 01:35:34,110
There was a cellist, I think.

1298
01:35:35,540 --> 01:35:36,600
I'm sorry.

1299
01:35:37,670 --> 01:35:39,580
He seemed like a good man.

1300
01:35:40,710 --> 01:35:41,700
He was an idiot.

1301
01:35:41,700 --> 01:35:43,850
Why? For believing?

1302
01:35:43,850 --> 01:35:45,320
For taking on Loki alone.

1303
01:35:45,770 --> 01:35:46,950
He was doing his job.

1304
01:35:47,510 --> 01:35:50,350
He was out of his league. He should have waited.

1305
01:35:50,350 --> 01:35:51,560
He should have...

1306
01:35:51,560 --> 01:35:53,170
Sometimes there isn't a way out, Tony.

1307
01:35:53,170 --> 01:35:54,860
Right, I've heard that before.

1308
01:35:55,330 --> 01:35:57,020
Is this the first time you lost a soldier?

1309
01:35:57,020 --> 01:35:58,830
We are not soldiers.

1310
01:36:03,110 --> 01:36:04,910
I'm not marching to Fury's fife.

1311
01:36:05,280 --> 01:36:06,240
Neither am I.

1312
01:36:06,240 --> 01:36:08,540
He's got the same blood on his hands that Loki does.

1313
01:36:08,540 --> 01:36:11,780
But right now, we got to behind us and get this done.

1314
01:36:12,330 --> 01:36:13,890
Loki needs a power source.

1315
01:36:13,890 --> 01:36:14,670
If we can put together a list...

1316
01:36:14,670 --> 01:36:15,570
He made it personal.

1317
01:36:16,040 --> 01:36:17,030
That's not the point.

1318
01:36:17,030 --> 01:36:19,520
That is the point. That's Loki's point.

1319
01:36:19,520 --> 01:36:21,690
He hit us all right where we live. Why?

1320
01:36:21,690 --> 01:36:22,580
To tear us apart.

1321
01:36:22,580 --> 01:36:24,780
Yeah, divide and conquer is great

1322
01:36:24,780 --> 01:36:27,320
but he knows he has to take us out to win, right?

1323
01:36:27,320 --> 01:36:28,710
That's what he wants.

1324
01:36:29,120 --> 01:36:31,350
He wants to beat us, he wants to be seen doing it.

1325
01:36:31,740 --> 01:36:33,100
He wants an audience.

1326
01:36:33,560 --> 01:36:35,260
Right. I caught his act in Stuttgart.

1327
01:36:35,260 --> 01:36:38,390
Yeah, that was just previews. This is opening night.

1328
01:36:38,390 --> 01:36:41,160
And Loki, he's a full-tilt diva, right?

1329
01:36:41,160 --> 01:36:42,800
He wants flowers, he wants parades.

1330
01:36:42,800 --> 01:36:46,150
He wants a monument built to the skies with his name plastered...

1331
01:36:48,260 --> 01:36:49,230
Son of a bitch.

1332
01:37:01,090 --> 01:37:01,770
Time to go.

1333
01:37:02,230 --> 01:37:02,970
Go where?

1334
01:37:02,970 --> 01:37:03,930
I'll tell you on the way.

1335
01:37:03,930 --> 01:37:05,230
Can you fly one of those jets?

1336
01:37:06,540 --> 01:37:07,340
I can.

1337
01:37:11,890 --> 01:37:12,880
You got a suit?

1338
01:37:12,920 --> 01:37:13,520
Yeah.

1339
01:37:13,990 --> 01:37:15,060
Then suit up.

1340
01:37:43,030 --> 01:37:44,660
Hey, you guys aren't authorised to be in here.

1341
01:37:44,660 --> 01:37:46,800
Son, just don't.

1342
01:37:48,990 --> 01:37:49,590
Sir.

1343
01:37:50,010 --> 01:37:51,140
Agent Hill.

1344
01:37:51,760 --> 01:37:53,460
Those cards,

1345
01:37:55,400 --> 01:37:59,200
they were in Coulson's locker, not in his jacket.

1346
01:38:04,270 --> 01:38:05,600
They needed the push.

1347
01:38:09,050 --> 01:38:11,370
We have an unauthorised departure from Bay 6.

1348
01:38:12,150 --> 01:38:13,280
They found him.

1349
01:38:14,370 --> 01:38:17,030
Get our communications back up, whatever you have to do.

1350
01:38:18,240 --> 01:38:19,540
I want eyes on everything.

1351
01:38:19,540 --> 01:38:20,140
Yes, sir.

1352
01:38:33,830 --> 01:38:35,870
Sir, I've turned off the arc reactor

1353
01:38:36,790 --> 01:38:39,210
but the device is already self-sustaining.

1354
01:38:39,820 --> 01:38:41,410
Shut it down, Dr Selvig.

1355
01:38:42,660 --> 01:38:43,760
It's too late!

1356
01:38:46,120 --> 01:38:47,390
She can't stop now.

1357
01:38:48,520 --> 01:38:50,280
She wants to show us something!

1358
01:38:51,290 --> 01:38:52,620
A new universe.

1359
01:38:53,310 --> 01:38:53,980
Okay.

1360
01:39:02,020 --> 01:39:03,410
The barrier is pure energy.

1361
01:39:04,280 --> 01:39:05,420
It's unbreachable.

1362
01:39:05,810 --> 01:39:06,840
Yeah, I got that.

1363
01:39:08,800 --> 01:39:09,700
Plan B.

1364
01:39:10,910 --> 01:39:13,170
Sir, the Mark 7 is not ready for deployment.

1365
01:39:13,170 --> 01:39:15,030
Then skip the spinning rims. We're on the clock.

1366
01:39:35,280 --> 01:39:37,970
Please tell me you're going to appeal to my humanity.

1367
01:39:39,450 --> 01:39:40,870
Actually, I'm planning to threaten you.

1368
01:39:41,760 --> 01:39:43,310
You should have left your armour on for that.

1369
01:39:43,310 --> 01:39:44,060
Yeah.

1370
01:39:45,060 --> 01:39:49,010
It's seen a bit of mileage, and you've got the glow stick of destiny.

1371
01:39:49,620 --> 01:39:50,480
Would you like a drink?

1372
01:39:51,960 --> 01:39:53,310
Stalling me won't change anything.

1373
01:39:53,310 --> 01:39:54,520
No, no. Threatening.

1374
01:39:55,610 --> 01:39:56,790
No drink? Are you sure?

1375
01:39:57,180 --> 01:39:58,120
I'm having one.

1376
01:39:59,650 --> 01:40:03,560
The Chitauri are coming. Nothing will change that.

1377
01:40:04,580 --> 01:40:05,690
What have I to fear?

1378
01:40:06,060 --> 01:40:07,160
The Avengers.

1379
01:40:09,680 --> 01:40:11,960
That's what we call ourselves. We're sort of like a team.

1380
01:40:11,960 --> 01:40:14,000
"Earth's mightiest heroes"-type thing.

1381
01:40:14,000 --> 01:40:15,740
Yes, I've met them.

1382
01:40:16,320 --> 01:40:16,940
Yeah.

1383
01:40:17,280 --> 01:40:19,580
It takes us a while to get any traction, I'll give you that one.

1384
01:40:19,580 --> 01:40:21,400
But let's do a head count, here.

1385
01:40:21,820 --> 01:40:23,770
Your brother, the demigod,

1386
01:40:26,160 --> 01:40:29,530
a super soldier, a living legend who kind of lives up to the legend.

1387
01:40:30,020 --> 01:40:33,160
A man with breathtaking anger-management issues,

1388
01:40:33,160 --> 01:40:36,210
a couple of master assassins, and you, big fella,

1389
01:40:36,980 --> 01:40:39,740
you've managed to piss off every single one of them.

1390
01:40:40,170 --> 01:40:41,080
That was the plan.

1391
01:40:41,080 --> 01:40:42,150
Not a great plan.

1392
01:40:43,130 --> 01:40:44,310
When they come,

1393
01:40:45,370 --> 01:40:47,040
and they will,

1394
01:40:47,040 --> 01:40:48,020
they'll come for you.

1395
01:40:48,350 --> 01:40:49,270
I have an army.

1396
01:40:49,270 --> 01:40:50,540
We have a Hulk.

1397
01:40:51,100 --> 01:40:52,630
I thought the beast had wandered off.

1398
01:40:52,630 --> 01:40:54,580
You're missing the point. There is no throne.

1399
01:40:54,580 --> 01:40:58,140
There is no version of this where you come out on top.

1400
01:40:58,730 --> 01:41:01,280
Maybe your army comes and maybe it's too much for us,

1401
01:41:01,280 --> 01:41:02,700
but it's all on you.

1402
01:41:04,090 --> 01:41:07,050
Because if we can't protect the Earth, you can be damn well sure we'll avenge it.

1403
01:41:10,380 --> 01:41:12,380
How will your friends have time for me

1404
01:41:13,610 --> 01:41:15,560
when they are so busy fighting you?

1405
01:41:23,100 --> 01:41:23,970
This usually works.

1406
01:41:23,970 --> 01:41:26,990
Well, performance issues, it's not uncommon.

1407
01:41:26,990 --> 01:41:27,570
One out of five...

1408
01:41:30,330 --> 01:41:32,580
Jarvis, anytime now.

1409
01:41:35,080 --> 01:41:37,750
You will all fall before me.

1410
01:41:38,160 --> 01:41:38,940
Deploy!

1411
01:41:39,360 --> 01:41:40,050
Deploy!

1412
01:42:08,040 --> 01:42:10,400
And there's one other person you pissed off.

1413
01:42:12,060 --> 01:42:13,210
His name was Phil.

1414
01:42:37,140 --> 01:42:37,760
Right.

1415
01:42:38,770 --> 01:42:39,570
Army.

1416
01:43:52,260 --> 01:43:53,260
Loki!

1417
01:43:53,740 --> 01:43:55,820
Turn off the Tesseract, or I'll destroy it.

1418
01:43:55,820 --> 01:43:56,650
You can't.

1419
01:43:57,090 --> 01:43:58,510
There is no stopping it.

1420
01:43:58,990 --> 01:44:00,140
There is only

1421
01:44:00,840 --> 01:44:01,970
the war.

1422
01:44:01,970 --> 01:44:02,990
So be it.

1423
01:44:25,770 --> 01:44:27,600
Stark, we're on your three, headed northeast.

1424
01:44:27,600 --> 01:44:29,230
What? Did you stop for drive-through?

1425
01:44:29,640 --> 01:44:31,230
Swing up Park. I'm going to lay them out for you.

1426
01:44:49,500 --> 01:44:51,030
Sir, we have more incoming.

1427
01:44:51,030 --> 01:44:52,610
Fine. Let's keep them occupied.

1428
01:44:59,690 --> 01:45:00,380
Nat?

1429
01:45:00,760 --> 01:45:01,640
I see him.

1430
01:45:45,920 --> 01:45:46,820
We got to get back up there.

1431
01:46:39,340 --> 01:46:40,570
Stark, are you seeing this?

1432
01:46:41,730 --> 01:46:44,010
Seeing. Still working on believing.

1433
01:46:44,010 --> 01:46:45,570
Where's Banner? Has he shown up yet?

1434
01:46:45,570 --> 01:46:46,300
Banner?

1435
01:46:46,970 --> 01:46:48,070
Just keep me posted.

1436
01:46:48,590 --> 01:46:50,450
Jarvis, find me a soft spot.

1437
01:46:53,320 --> 01:46:54,240
Look at this!

1438
01:46:55,190 --> 01:46:56,390
Look around you!

1439
01:46:57,170 --> 01:47:00,070
You think this madness will end with your rule?

1440
01:47:01,060 --> 01:47:02,220
It's too late.

1441
01:47:04,110 --> 01:47:05,650
It's too late to stop it.

1442
01:47:05,650 --> 01:47:09,140
No. We can, together.

1443
01:47:16,090 --> 01:47:17,670
Sentiment.

1444
01:47:45,960 --> 01:47:47,410
We've got civilians still trapped up here.

1445
01:47:49,470 --> 01:47:50,360
Loki.

1446
01:48:01,740 --> 01:48:03,140
They're fish in a barrel down there.

1447
01:48:09,320 --> 01:48:10,800
We got this. It's good. Go.

1448
01:48:11,360 --> 01:48:12,400
Do you think you can hold them off?

1449
01:48:12,990 --> 01:48:13,940
Captain,

1450
01:48:15,810 --> 01:48:17,360
it would be my genuine pleasure.

1451
01:48:45,490 --> 01:48:47,520
Just like Budapest all over again.

1452
01:48:47,910 --> 01:48:50,250
You and I remember Budapest very differently.

1453
01:49:06,970 --> 01:49:09,050
It's going to be an hour before they can scramble the National Guard.

1454
01:49:09,050 --> 01:49:09,700
National Guard?

1455
01:49:11,860 --> 01:49:13,450
Does the army know what's happening here?

1456
01:49:14,180 --> 01:49:14,950
Do we?

1457
01:49:15,880 --> 01:49:17,150
You need men in these buildings.

1458
01:49:17,150 --> 01:49:20,050
There are people inside and they're going to be running right into the line of fire.

1459
01:49:20,050 --> 01:49:23,870
You take them to the basements or through the subway. You keep them off the streets.

1460
01:49:23,870 --> 01:49:26,490
I need a perimeter as far back as 39th.

1461
01:49:26,490 --> 01:49:28,410
Why the hell should I take orders from you?

1462
01:49:42,290 --> 01:49:43,620
I need men in those buildings.

1463
01:49:43,620 --> 01:49:45,520
Lead the people down and away from the streets.

1464
01:49:45,850 --> 01:49:48,340
We're going to set up a perimeter all the way down to 39th Street.

1465
01:49:58,690 --> 01:50:00,810
Well, we got its attention.

1466
01:50:00,810 --> 01:50:01,680
What the hell was step two?

1467
01:50:31,940 --> 01:50:32,950
What's the story upstairs?

1468
01:50:32,950 --> 01:50:35,170
The power surrounding the Cube is impenetrable.

1469
01:50:35,170 --> 01:50:37,230
Thor's right. We got to deal with these guys.

1470
01:50:37,730 --> 01:50:38,680
How do we do this?

1471
01:50:38,680 --> 01:50:39,510
As a team.

1472
01:50:39,510 --> 01:50:41,160
I have unfinished business with Loki.

1473
01:50:41,530 --> 01:50:42,730
Yeah? Well, get in line.

1474
01:50:42,730 --> 01:50:43,800
Save it.

1475
01:50:43,800 --> 01:50:45,220
Loki's going to keep this fight focused on us,

1476
01:50:45,220 --> 01:50:46,220
and that's what we need.

1477
01:50:46,220 --> 01:50:48,000
Without him, these things could run wild.

1478
01:50:48,000 --> 01:50:50,450
We got Stark up top. He's going to need us to...

1479
01:50:58,540 --> 01:51:02,000
So, this all seems horrible.

1480
01:51:02,760 --> 01:51:03,940
I've seen worse.

1481
01:51:04,510 --> 01:51:05,140
Sorry.

1482
01:51:05,400 --> 01:51:08,410
No, we could use a little worse.

1483
01:51:08,410 --> 01:51:10,150
Stark, we got him.

1484
01:51:10,150 --> 01:51:10,980
Banner?

1485
01:51:10,980 --> 01:51:12,230
Just like you said.

1486
01:51:12,230 --> 01:51:15,080
Then tell him to suit up. I'm bringing the party to you.

1487
01:51:21,590 --> 01:51:23,390
I don't see how that's a party.

1488
01:51:31,590 --> 01:51:32,390
Dr Banner.

1489
01:51:34,070 --> 01:51:36,020
Now might be a really good time for you to get angry.

1490
01:51:36,840 --> 01:51:38,250
That's my secret, Captain.

1491
01:51:40,980 --> 01:51:42,140
I'm always angry.

1492
01:51:53,970 --> 01:51:54,860
Hold on!

1493
01:52:25,340 --> 01:52:26,800
Send the rest.

1494
01:52:33,640 --> 01:52:34,500
Guys.

1495
01:52:35,100 --> 01:52:36,180
Call it, Captain.

1496
01:52:36,180 --> 01:52:36,990
All right, listen up.

1497
01:52:37,700 --> 01:52:40,130
Until we can close that portal, our priority is containment.

1498
01:52:40,550 --> 01:52:42,010
Barton, I want you on that roof.

1499
01:52:42,010 --> 01:52:43,970
Eyes on everything. Call out patterns and strays.

1500
01:52:43,970 --> 01:52:45,440
Stark, you got the perimeter.

1501
01:52:45,440 --> 01:52:48,500
Anything gets more than three blocks out, you turn it back or you turn it to ash.

1502
01:52:48,500 --> 01:52:49,340
Can you give me a lift?

1503
01:52:49,340 --> 01:52:51,050
Right. Better clench up, Legolas.

1504
01:52:54,500 --> 01:52:57,990
Thor, you got to try and bottleneck that portal. Slow them down.

1505
01:52:58,310 --> 01:53:00,450
You got the lightning. Light the bastards up.

1506
01:53:02,920 --> 01:53:05,490
You and me, we stay here on the ground. We keep the fighting here.

1507
01:53:05,910 --> 01:53:06,590
And Hulk...

1508
01:53:09,340 --> 01:53:10,180
Smash.

1509
01:54:03,970 --> 01:54:04,610
Sir.

1510
01:54:06,210 --> 01:54:06,770
The Council is on.

1511
01:54:12,360 --> 01:54:14,970
Stark, you got a lot of strays sniffing your tail.

1512
01:54:17,050 --> 01:54:19,210
I'm just trying to keep them off the streets.

1513
01:54:19,210 --> 01:54:20,740
Well, they can't bank worth a damn.

1514
01:54:21,920 --> 01:54:23,050
So find a tight corner.

1515
01:54:23,050 --> 01:54:24,270
I will roger that.

1516
01:54:47,420 --> 01:54:48,680
Oh, boy.

1517
01:54:55,690 --> 01:54:56,540
Nice call.

1518
01:54:57,410 --> 01:54:58,320
What else you got?

1519
01:54:58,670 --> 01:55:00,780
Thor is taking on a squadron down on Sixth.

1520
01:55:01,610 --> 01:55:03,390
And he didn't invite me.

1521
01:55:43,400 --> 01:55:46,270
Captain, none of this is going to mean a damn thing if we don't close that portal.

1522
01:55:46,270 --> 01:55:47,610
Our biggest guns couldn't touch it.

1523
01:55:48,030 --> 01:55:49,420
Well, maybe it's not about guns.

1524
01:55:52,530 --> 01:55:54,160
If you want to get up there, you're going to need a ride.

1525
01:55:55,580 --> 01:55:56,410
I got a ride.

1526
01:55:57,690 --> 01:55:58,890
I could use a boost, though.

1527
01:56:01,560 --> 01:56:02,420
Are you sure about this?

1528
01:56:02,760 --> 01:56:04,460
Yeah. It's gonna be fun.

1529
01:56:32,330 --> 01:56:33,650
Okay, turn, turn.

1530
01:56:33,960 --> 01:56:35,550
Less! Less!

1531
01:57:58,760 --> 01:58:01,430
Captain, the bank on 42nd past Madison.

1532
01:58:01,790 --> 01:58:03,290
They've cornered a lot of civilians in there.

1533
01:58:03,680 --> 01:58:04,640
I'm on it.

1534
01:58:25,610 --> 01:58:26,790
Everyone! Clear out!

1535
01:58:57,390 --> 01:58:58,760
Director Fury,

1536
01:58:59,190 --> 01:59:00,820
the Council has made a decision.

1537
01:59:00,880 --> 01:59:03,910
I recognise the Council has made a decision.

1538
01:59:03,910 --> 01:59:05,850
But given that it's a stupid-ass decision,

1539
01:59:05,940 --> 01:59:07,280
I have elected to ignore it.

1540
01:59:07,280 --> 01:59:10,910
Director, you're closer than any of our subs.

1541
01:59:10,910 --> 01:59:11,970
You scramble that jet...

1542
01:59:11,970 --> 01:59:14,680
That is the island of Manhattan, Councilman.

1543
01:59:14,680 --> 01:59:16,870
Until I'm certain my team can't hold it,

1544
01:59:16,870 --> 01:59:20,610
I will not order a nuclear strike against a civilian population.

1545
01:59:20,610 --> 01:59:22,940
If we don't hold them here, we lose everything.

1546
01:59:22,940 --> 01:59:25,160
If I send that bird out, we already have.

1547
01:59:29,490 --> 01:59:30,790
You.

1548
01:59:33,580 --> 01:59:34,330
Hawkeye!

1549
01:59:36,000 --> 01:59:37,180
Nat, what are you doing?

1550
01:59:38,180 --> 01:59:39,060
A little help?

1551
01:59:44,640 --> 01:59:45,690
I got him.

1552
02:00:12,220 --> 02:00:13,090
Enough!

1553
02:00:13,500 --> 02:00:15,510
You are, all of you, beneath me!

1554
02:00:15,920 --> 02:00:18,190
I am a god, you dull creature.

1555
02:00:18,710 --> 02:00:20,170
And I will not be bullied by...

1556
02:00:29,960 --> 02:00:31,170
Puny god.

1557
02:00:40,130 --> 02:00:41,220
The sceptre...

1558
02:00:42,730 --> 02:00:43,570
Doctor.

1559
02:00:45,800 --> 02:00:48,360
Loki's sceptre. The energy.

1560
02:00:48,830 --> 02:00:50,520
The Tesseract can't fight,

1561
02:00:50,520 --> 02:00:52,720
but you can't protect against yourself.

1562
02:00:52,720 --> 02:00:54,940
It's not your fault. You didn't know what you were doing.

1563
02:00:58,130 --> 02:00:59,670
Actually, I think I did.

1564
02:01:00,420 --> 02:01:02,650
I built in a safety to cut their power source.

1565
02:01:04,640 --> 02:01:06,050
Loki's sceptre.

1566
02:01:06,400 --> 02:01:08,240
It may be able to close the portal.

1567
02:01:10,920 --> 02:01:12,770
And I'm looking right at it.

1568
02:01:25,440 --> 02:01:27,780
Sir, we will lose power before we penetrate that shell.

1569
02:01:35,460 --> 02:01:38,910
Jarvis, you ever hear the tale of Jonah?

1570
02:01:39,220 --> 02:01:41,250
I wouldn't consider him a role model.

1571
02:02:50,860 --> 02:02:52,780
Director Fury is no longer in command.

1572
02:02:52,780 --> 02:02:54,730
Override order 7-Alpha- 1- 1.

1573
02:02:55,070 --> 02:02:57,470
7- Alpha- 1- 1, confirmed. We're go for takeoff.

1574
02:02:58,410 --> 02:03:00,480
Sir, we have a bird in motion!

1575
02:03:00,980 --> 02:03:03,070
Anyone on the deck, we have a rogue bird.

1576
02:03:03,070 --> 02:03:04,340
We need to shut it down!

1577
02:03:04,340 --> 02:03:06,710
Repeat, takeoff is not authorised.

1578
02:03:37,300 --> 02:03:38,800
Stark, do you hear me?

1579
02:03:39,590 --> 02:03:41,790
You have a missile headed straight for the city.

1580
02:03:42,200 --> 02:03:42,770
How long?

1581
02:03:43,860 --> 02:03:45,380
Three minutes, max.

1582
02:03:45,960 --> 02:03:47,620
The payload will wipe out Midtown.

1583
02:03:47,980 --> 02:03:49,890
Jarvis, put everything we got into the thrusters.

1584
02:03:49,890 --> 02:03:50,770
I just did.

1585
02:04:04,460 --> 02:04:05,550
Package is sent.

1586
02:04:06,340 --> 02:04:09,060
Detonation in 2 minutes, 30 seconds, mark.

1587
02:04:31,870 --> 02:04:32,970
Are you ready for another bout?

1588
02:04:34,930 --> 02:04:36,120
What, are you getting sleepy?

1589
02:04:41,550 --> 02:04:42,620
Right at the crown!

1590
02:04:49,290 --> 02:04:50,370
I can close it.

1591
02:04:51,220 --> 02:04:52,290
Can anybody copy?

1592
02:04:53,270 --> 02:04:54,590
I can shut the portal down.

1593
02:04:54,940 --> 02:04:55,630
Do it!

1594
02:04:55,630 --> 02:04:56,630
No, wait.

1595
02:04:56,630 --> 02:04:58,100
Stark, these things are still coming.

1596
02:04:58,100 --> 02:05:00,440
I got a nuke coming in. It's gonna blow in less than a minute.

1597
02:05:11,020 --> 02:05:12,620
And I know just where to put it.

1598
02:05:19,710 --> 02:05:22,430
Stark, you know that's a one-way trip.

1599
02:05:22,430 --> 02:05:23,880
Save the rest for the turn, J.

1600
02:05:23,880 --> 02:05:26,940
Sir, shall I try Miss Potts?

1601
02:05:28,110 --> 02:05:29,070
Might as well.

1602
02:05:32,070 --> 02:05:34,660
The streets of New York City have become a battleground.

1603
02:05:34,660 --> 02:05:37,390
The Army is here trying to contain the violence

1604
02:05:37,390 --> 02:05:39,350
but clearly, it is outmatched.

1605
02:05:39,350 --> 02:05:43,900
And I have to say, in all my years of reporting, I have never seen anything like this.

1606
02:05:44,880 --> 02:05:46,300
We have limited information on the team

1607
02:05:46,300 --> 02:05:49,680
but we do know that billionaire Tony Stark's Iron Man...

1608
02:07:03,400 --> 02:07:04,650
Come on, Stark.

1609
02:07:11,700 --> 02:07:12,610
Close it.

1610
02:07:32,790 --> 02:07:33,830
Son of a gun.

1611
02:07:38,660 --> 02:07:39,890
He's not slowing down.

1612
02:07:58,280 --> 02:07:59,430
Is he breathing?

1613
02:08:27,650 --> 02:08:28,690
What the hell?

1614
02:08:31,720 --> 02:08:32,650
What just happened?

1615
02:08:33,690 --> 02:08:34,940
Please tell me nobody kissed me.

1616
02:08:40,570 --> 02:08:41,500
We won.

1617
02:08:44,590 --> 02:08:45,600
All right, yay!

1618
02:08:46,070 --> 02:08:47,690
Hurray. Good job, guys.

1619
02:08:48,150 --> 02:08:51,260
Let's just not come in tomorrow. Let's just take a day.

1620
02:08:52,250 --> 02:08:53,530
Have you ever tried shawarma?

1621
02:08:54,230 --> 02:08:56,530
There's a shawarma joint about two blocks from here.

1622
02:08:56,530 --> 02:08:58,400
I don't know what it is, but I want to try it.

1623
02:08:58,710 --> 02:09:00,050
We're not finished yet.

1624
02:09:05,040 --> 02:09:06,340
And then shawarma after.

1625
02:09:28,900 --> 02:09:30,320
If it's all the same to you,

1626
02:09:34,500 --> 02:09:36,000
I'll have that drink now.

1627
02:09:44,050 --> 02:09:47,970
Despite the devastation of what has been confirmed as an extraterrestrial attack,

1628
02:09:47,970 --> 02:09:51,680
the extraordinary heroics of the group known as the Avengers

1629
02:09:51,680 --> 02:09:55,330
has been to many a cause not only for comfort, but for celebration.

1630
02:09:55,330 --> 02:09:56,490
It's just really great knowing they're out there.

1631
02:09:57,110 --> 02:09:58,420
That someone is watching over us.

1632
02:09:59,100 --> 02:10:00,160
I love you, Thor!

1633
02:10:00,160 --> 02:10:02,110
And then these guys were like...

1634
02:10:02,110 --> 02:10:03,660
And then the air goes...

1635
02:10:03,660 --> 02:10:05,940
And this green guy walks up and he goes...

1636
02:10:05,940 --> 02:10:08,910
I don't know .I don't exactly feel safer with those things out there.

1637
02:10:08,910 --> 02:10:12,050
It just seems that there's a lot they're not telling us.

1638
02:10:12,050 --> 02:10:15,590
Superheroes in New York? Give me a break.

1639
02:10:15,590 --> 02:10:17,660
These so-called "heroes"

1640
02:10:17,660 --> 02:10:21,140
have to be held responsible for the destruction done to this city.

1641
02:10:21,500 --> 02:10:23,710
This was their fight. Where are they now?

1642
02:10:23,710 --> 02:10:26,650
Tough questions are being asked about the Avengers themselves.

1643
02:10:26,650 --> 02:10:29,200
Their sudden appearance and equally sudden disappearance..

1644
02:10:29,200 --> 02:10:31,780
What, this is all somehow their fault?

1645
02:10:34,070 --> 02:10:36,900
Captain America saved my life.

1646
02:10:39,360 --> 02:10:42,960
Wherever he is, and wherever any of them are,

1647
02:10:42,960 --> 02:10:44,090
I would just...

1648
02:10:45,330 --> 02:10:47,280
I would want to say thank you.

1649
02:10:50,090 --> 02:10:51,510
Where are the Avengers?

1650
02:10:51,510 --> 02:10:54,130
I'm not currently tracking their whereabouts.

1651
02:10:54,130 --> 02:10:56,500
I'd say they've earned a leave of absence.

1652
02:10:56,500 --> 02:10:57,790
And the Tesseract?

1653
02:10:58,220 --> 02:11:00,180
The Tesseract is where it belongs.

1654
02:11:00,900 --> 02:11:02,630
Out of our reach.

1655
02:11:03,350 --> 02:11:04,840
That's not your call.

1656
02:11:04,840 --> 02:11:06,030
I didn't make it.

1657
02:11:06,030 --> 02:11:08,550
I just didn't argue with the god that did.

1658
02:11:08,550 --> 02:11:10,500
So, you let him take it

1659
02:11:10,500 --> 02:11:14,020
and the war criminal, Loki,who should be answering for his crime.

1660
02:11:14,300 --> 02:11:16,460
I think he will be.

1661
02:11:30,270 --> 02:11:32,770
I don't think you understand what you've started,

1662
02:11:33,150 --> 02:11:35,030
letting the Avengers loose on this world.

1663
02:11:35,950 --> 02:11:36,920
They're dangerous.

1664
02:11:37,250 --> 02:11:40,790
They surely are, and the whole world knows it.

1665
02:11:41,290 --> 02:11:43,830
Every world knows it.

1666
02:11:44,310 --> 02:11:46,350
Was that the point of all this?

1667
02:11:46,760 --> 02:11:47,910
A statement?

1668
02:11:50,890 --> 02:11:52,160
A promise.

1669
02:12:01,190 --> 02:12:02,560
Sir, how does it work now?

1670
02:12:03,750 --> 02:12:05,220
They've gone their separate ways.

1671
02:12:05,800 --> 02:12:08,250
Some, pretty extremely far.

1672
02:12:09,650 --> 02:12:12,810
If we get into a situation like this again, what happens then?

1673
02:12:13,350 --> 02:12:14,560
They'll come back.

1674
02:12:15,840 --> 02:12:17,170
Are you really sure about that?

1675
02:12:17,660 --> 02:12:18,840
I am.

1676
02:12:20,230 --> 02:12:21,030
Why?

1677
02:12:22,520 --> 02:12:24,720
Because we'll need them to.

1678
02:15:16,800 --> 02:15:18,900
Humans.

1679
02:15:20,070 --> 02:15:24,790
They are not the cowering wretches we were promised.

1680
02:15:25,380 --> 02:15:27,610
They stand.

1681
02:15:28,420 --> 02:15:34,440
They are unruly, and therefore cannot be ruled.

1682
02:15:41,830 --> 02:15:44,510
To challenge them

1683
02:15:44,920 --> 02:15:48,590
is to court death.

